1
00:01:16,702 --> 00:01:20,445
GANDALF: <i>You cannot pass!</i>
FRODO: <i>Gandalf!</i>

2
00:01:25,294 --> 00:01:30,630
GANDALF: <i>I am a servant of the Secret Fire,</i>
<i>wielder of the flame of Anor.</i>

3
00:01:38,599 --> 00:01:41,341
<i>Go back to the Shadow.</i>

4
00:01:42,269 --> 00:01:46,057
<i>The dark fire will not avail you,</i>
<i>flame of Udûn!</i>

5
00:01:49,901 --> 00:01:54,486
You shall not pass!

6
00:02:00,412 --> 00:02:01,993
[ROARING]

7
00:02:16,178 --> 00:02:18,009
[GRUNTS]

8
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:23,386
BOROMIR:
No! No!

9
00:02:23,477 --> 00:02:25,513
Gandalf!

10
00:02:33,028 --> 00:02:34,768
Fly, you fools.

11
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:37,270
No!

12
00:02:39,242 --> 00:02:41,324
Gandalf!

13
00:02:57,427 --> 00:03:01,545
[ROARING AND YELLING]

14
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:51,811
Gandalf!

15
00:03:52,816 --> 00:03:55,102
What is it, Mr. Frodo?

16
00:03:56,987 --> 00:03:58,727
Nothing.

17
00:04:06,037 --> 00:04:08,119
Just a dream.

18
00:04:21,261 --> 00:04:22,467
Can you see the bottom?

19
00:04:23,764 --> 00:04:26,881
No! Don't look down, Sam!
Just keep going!

20
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:35,730
[GRUNTS]

21
00:04:37,694 --> 00:04:39,855
Catch it! Grab it, Mr. Frodo!

22
00:04:41,490 --> 00:04:42,821
[YELLS]

23
00:04:42,908 --> 00:04:44,899
Mr. Frodo!

24
00:04:47,496 --> 00:04:49,236
I think I've found the bottom.

25
00:04:54,669 --> 00:04:57,661
SAM: Bogs and rope,
and goodness knows what.

26
00:04:57,756 --> 00:05:01,044
It's not natural. None of it.

27
00:05:04,221 --> 00:05:06,303
-What's in this?
-Nothing.

28
00:05:07,682 --> 00:05:08,717
Just a bit of seasoning.

29
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:12,176
I thought maybe if we was having
a roast chicken one night or something.

30
00:05:12,687 --> 00:05:14,848
Roast chicken?!

31
00:05:15,482 --> 00:05:16,722
You never know.

32
00:05:17,192 --> 00:05:20,184
Sam. My dear Sam.

33
00:05:21,822 --> 00:05:25,781
It's very special, that.
It's the best salt in all the Shire.

34
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:29,026
It is special.

35
00:05:32,916 --> 00:05:34,827
It's a little bit of home.

36
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:40,541
We can't leave this here for someone
to follow us down.

37
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:44,499
Who's gonna follow us down here,
Mr. Frodo?

38
00:05:45,345 --> 00:05:49,213
It's a shame, really.
Lady Galadriel gave me that.

39
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:51,806
Real Elvish rope.

40
00:05:52,727 --> 00:05:55,139
Well, there's nothing for it.
It's one of my knots.

41
00:05:55,230 --> 00:05:57,221
Won't come free in a hurry.

42
00:06:06,241 --> 00:06:08,323
Real Elvish rope.

43
00:06:22,424 --> 00:06:26,963
Mordor. The one place in Middle-earth
we don't want to see any closer.

44
00:06:27,053 --> 00:06:29,294
And it's the one place
we're trying to get to.

45
00:06:30,056 --> 00:06:31,796
It's just where we can't get.

46
00:06:33,268 --> 00:06:36,260
Let's face it, Mr. Frodo, we're lost.

47
00:06:38,565 --> 00:06:41,307
I don't think Gandalf meant for us to
come this way.

48
00:06:42,944 --> 00:06:46,277
He didn't mean for a lot of things
to happen, Sam...

49
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:48,563
...but they did.

50
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:57,952
[RUMBLING]

51
00:06:58,043 --> 00:07:00,455
[GASPING]

52
00:07:01,630 --> 00:07:02,665
Mr. Frodo?

53
00:07:06,593 --> 00:07:08,003
It's the Ring, isn't it?

54
00:07:09,095 --> 00:07:11,586
It's getting heavier.

55
00:07:24,194 --> 00:07:26,936
-What food have we got left?
-Let me see.

56
00:07:27,656 --> 00:07:29,772
Oh, yes. Lovely.

57
00:07:29,866 --> 00:07:32,653
Lembas bread. And look!

58
00:07:35,121 --> 00:07:37,362
More lembas bread.

59
00:07:48,134 --> 00:07:50,090
I don't usually hold with foreign food...

60
00:07:50,345 --> 00:07:53,257
...but this Elvish stuff, it's not bad.

61
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:57,632
Nothing ever dampens your spirits,
does it, Sam?

62
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:05,769
Those rain clouds might.

63
00:08:09,239 --> 00:08:11,696
[THUNDER ROLLING]

64
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:42,807
SAM:
This looks strangely familiar.

65
00:08:43,398 --> 00:08:45,935
It's because we've been here before.

66
00:08:46,026 --> 00:08:48,642
We're going in circles.

67
00:08:49,404 --> 00:08:51,269
SAM:
What is that horrid stink?

68
00:08:51,364 --> 00:08:53,650
I warrant there's a nasty bog nearby.

69
00:08:53,742 --> 00:08:55,698
-Can you smell it?
-Yes.

70
00:08:57,746 --> 00:08:59,987
I can smell it.

71
00:09:03,251 --> 00:09:05,708
We're not alone.

72
00:09:19,350 --> 00:09:23,468
The thieves. The thieves.

73
00:09:23,563 --> 00:09:27,556
The filthy little thieves.

74
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:30,441
Where is it?

75
00:09:30,528 --> 00:09:33,270
Where is it?

76
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:37,236
They stole it from us.

77
00:09:37,327 --> 00:09:41,570
My precious.

78
00:09:42,457 --> 00:09:45,745
Curse them, we hates them!

79
00:09:45,835 --> 00:09:49,953
It's ours, it is, and we wants it!

80
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:53,173
[YELLING]

81
00:10:30,171 --> 00:10:32,503
[SAM YELLS]

82
00:10:45,019 --> 00:10:46,884
This is Sting.

83
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:48,561
You've seen it before...

84
00:10:48,648 --> 00:10:51,185
...haven't you, Gollum?

85
00:10:55,238 --> 00:10:58,730
Release him or I'll cut your throat.

86
00:11:00,869 --> 00:11:02,609
[SIGHS]

87
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:07,329
[WHIMPERS]

88
00:11:10,253 --> 00:11:12,118
[GOLLUM SCREAMING]

89
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:16,630
It burns!

90
00:11:16,718 --> 00:11:19,050
It burns us!

91
00:11:20,555 --> 00:11:22,011
It freezes!

92
00:11:23,808 --> 00:11:26,094
Nasty Elves twisted it.

93
00:11:26,186 --> 00:11:28,893
-Take it off us!
-Quiet, you!

94
00:11:32,317 --> 00:11:36,606
It's hopeless. Every Orc in Mordor's
going to hear this racket.

95
00:11:36,696 --> 00:11:39,358
-Let's just tie him up and leave him.
-No!

96
00:11:39,616 --> 00:11:43,154
That would kill us! Kill us!

97
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:45,986
It's no more than you deserve!

98
00:11:47,665 --> 00:11:49,701
Maybe he does deserve to die.

99
00:11:52,086 --> 00:11:55,578
But now that I see him, I do pity him.

100
00:11:59,010 --> 00:12:03,879
We be nice to them
if they be nice to us.

101
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:06,882
Take it off us.

102
00:12:10,021 --> 00:12:13,980
We swears to do what you wants.

103
00:12:14,067 --> 00:12:16,058
We swears.

104
00:12:16,361 --> 00:12:18,773
There's no promise you can make
that I can trust.

105
00:12:21,449 --> 00:12:23,314
We swears...

106
00:12:23,409 --> 00:12:28,199
...to serve the master
of the precious.

107
00:12:29,832 --> 00:12:32,198
We will swear on...

108
00:12:32,293 --> 00:12:34,329
...on the precious.

109
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:36,706
Gollum. Gollum.

110
00:12:36,798 --> 00:12:40,962
The Ring is treacherous.
It will hold you to your word.

111
00:12:41,803 --> 00:12:43,134
Yes...

112
00:12:43,721 --> 00:12:46,212
...on the precious.

113
00:12:48,643 --> 00:12:51,009
On the precious.

114
00:12:52,188 --> 00:12:53,678
I don't believe you!

115
00:12:55,692 --> 00:12:59,276
-Get down! I said, down!
-Sam!

116
00:12:59,362 --> 00:13:01,148
He's trying to trick us.

117
00:13:01,239 --> 00:13:04,356
If we let him go, he'll throttle us
in our sleep.

118
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:06,987
[WHEEZING]

119
00:13:15,753 --> 00:13:20,292
-You know the way to Mordor?
-Yes.

120
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:24,959
You've been there before?

121
00:13:25,972 --> 00:13:27,553
Yes.

122
00:13:38,443 --> 00:13:41,059
You will lead us to the Black Gate.

123
00:13:49,704 --> 00:13:53,572
SMÉAGOL: To the Gate, to the Gate!
To the Gate, the master says. Yes!

124
00:13:53,666 --> 00:13:58,581
GOLLUM: No! We won't go back.
Not there. Not to him.

125
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:03,005
They can't make us. Gollum! Gollum!

126
00:14:03,092 --> 00:14:06,630
But we swore to serve the master
of the precious.

127
00:14:06,721 --> 00:14:12,762
No. Ashes and dust and thirst there is,
and pits, pits, pits.

128
00:14:12,852 --> 00:14:15,810
And Orcses, thousands of Orcses.

129
00:14:15,897 --> 00:14:21,062
And always the Great Eye watching,
watching.

130
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:27,864
Hey! Come back now! Come back!

131
00:14:30,244 --> 00:14:32,530
There! What did I tell you?

132
00:14:32,622 --> 00:14:34,908
He's run off, the old villain.

133
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:37,615
So much for his promises.

134
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:39,450
SMÉAGOL:
This way, Hobbits.

135
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:41,661
Follow me!

136
00:14:55,478 --> 00:14:56,888
PIPPIN:
Merry!

137
00:14:57,855 --> 00:14:59,345
Merry!

138
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:08,738
You're late.
Our master grows impatient.

139
00:15:08,825 --> 00:15:10,690
He wants the Shire-rats now.

140
00:15:11,536 --> 00:15:16,121
I don't take orders from Orc-maggots.

141
00:15:17,166 --> 00:15:20,283
Saruman will have his prize.

142
00:15:20,378 --> 00:15:23,586
We will deliver them.

143
00:15:29,804 --> 00:15:31,169
Merry!

144
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:33,671
Merry? Wake up.

145
00:15:37,145 --> 00:15:39,010
My friend is sick.

146
00:15:39,439 --> 00:15:42,101
He needs water. Please!

147
00:15:42,859 --> 00:15:46,852
Sick, is he?
Give him some medicine, boys!

148
00:15:46,946 --> 00:15:48,937
[LAUGHING]

149
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:51,693
Stop it!

150
00:15:53,911 --> 00:15:56,527
Can't take his draught!

151
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:01,824
-Leave him alone!
-Why?

152
00:16:02,336 --> 00:16:05,328
You want some? Huh?

153
00:16:05,423 --> 00:16:08,836
Then keep your mouth shut.

154
00:16:12,263 --> 00:16:14,345
Merry.

155
00:16:15,141 --> 00:16:16,677
Hello, Pip.

156
00:16:18,478 --> 00:16:20,969
-You're hurt.
-I'm fine.

157
00:16:21,063 --> 00:16:23,645
-It was just an act.
-An act?

158
00:16:24,275 --> 00:16:27,142
See? I fooled you too.

159
00:16:29,864 --> 00:16:31,570
Don't worry about me, Pippin.

160
00:16:33,868 --> 00:16:35,859
What is it? What do you smell?

161
00:16:36,871 --> 00:16:38,156
Man-flesh.

162
00:16:40,291 --> 00:16:42,657
They've picked up our trail.

163
00:16:43,753 --> 00:16:44,868
Aragorn.

164
00:16:46,589 --> 00:16:48,420
Let's move!

165
00:17:09,779 --> 00:17:11,895
[RUMBLING]

166
00:17:11,989 --> 00:17:14,526
Their pace has quickened.

167
00:17:15,535 --> 00:17:17,571
They must have caught our scent.

168
00:17:17,662 --> 00:17:19,448
Hurry!

169
00:17:23,084 --> 00:17:24,870
Come on, Gimli!

170
00:17:28,673 --> 00:17:31,005
Three days and nights pursuit.

171
00:17:31,092 --> 00:17:34,129
No food. No rest.

172
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:38,259
And no sign of our quarry,
but what bare rock can tell.

173
00:18:09,714 --> 00:18:12,956
Not idly do the leaves of Lórien fall.

174
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:16,592
They may yet be alive.

175
00:18:17,471 --> 00:18:20,087
Less than a day ahead of us. Come.

176
00:18:22,685 --> 00:18:25,222
Come, Gimli! We're gaining on them!

177
00:18:25,313 --> 00:18:29,647
I'm wasted on cross-country.
We Dwarves are natural sprinters.

178
00:18:30,151 --> 00:18:33,484
Very dangerous over short distances.

179
00:18:45,166 --> 00:18:46,952
ARAGORN:
Rohan.

180
00:18:47,043 --> 00:18:49,876
Home of the Horse-lords.

181
00:18:51,088 --> 00:18:53,670
There's something strange at work here.

182
00:18:53,758 --> 00:18:56,875
Some evil gives speed
to these creatures.

183
00:18:56,969 --> 00:18:59,927
Sets its will against us.

184
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:08,056
ARAGORN:
Legolas! What do your Elf-eyes see?

185
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:10,763
LEGOLAS:
The Uruks turn northeast.

186
00:19:11,609 --> 00:19:13,770
They are taking the Hobbits to Isengard.

187
00:19:14,654 --> 00:19:15,894
Saruman.

188
00:19:24,330 --> 00:19:27,538
SARUMAN:
<i>The world is changing.</i>

189
00:19:27,625 --> 00:19:33,291
<i>Who now has the strength to stand</i>
<i>against the armies of Isengard...</i>

190
00:19:33,964 --> 00:19:36,706
<i>...and Mordor?</i>

191
00:19:38,386 --> 00:19:44,052
<i>To stand against the might of Sauron</i>
<i>and Saruman...</i>

192
00:19:44,141 --> 00:19:47,850
<i>...and the union of the two towers?</i>

193
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:57,352
<i>Together, my Lord Sauron...</i>

194
00:19:57,446 --> 00:20:01,064
<i>...we shall rule this Middle-earth.</i>

195
00:20:11,293 --> 00:20:13,158
[YELLING AND SQUEALING]

196
00:20:17,091 --> 00:20:21,334
SARUMAN: <i>The Old World will burn</i>
<i>in the fires of industry.</i>

197
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:25,175
<i>The forests will fall.</i>

198
00:20:27,101 --> 00:20:29,934
<i>A new order will rise.</i>

199
00:20:31,021 --> 00:20:35,981
<i>We will drive the machine of war</i>
<i>with the sword and the spear...</i>

200
00:20:36,068 --> 00:20:40,107
<i>...and the iron fists of the Orc.</i>

201
00:20:52,543 --> 00:20:55,785
SARUMAN: I want them armed
and ready to march within two weeks!

202
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:57,620
ORC:
But, my lord, there are too many!

203
00:20:57,715 --> 00:21:00,798
We cannot all be armed in time,
we don't have the means.

204
00:21:00,885 --> 00:21:04,127
Build a dam, block the stream,
work the furnaces night and day.

205
00:21:04,722 --> 00:21:07,134
We don't have enough fuel
to feed the fires.

206
00:21:08,434 --> 00:21:12,723
The Forest of Fangorn
lies on our doorstep.

207
00:21:14,148 --> 00:21:16,480
-Burn it.
-Yes.

208
00:21:17,193 --> 00:21:19,525
WILD MAN:
We will fight for you.

209
00:21:19,612 --> 00:21:21,648
Swear it.

210
00:21:32,166 --> 00:21:36,910
We will die for Saruman.

211
00:21:38,005 --> 00:21:40,041
SARUMAN:
The Horse-Men took your lands.

212
00:21:40,132 --> 00:21:44,751
They drove your people into the hills
to scratch a living off rocks.

213
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:46,301
Murderers!

214
00:21:47,223 --> 00:21:49,384
SARUMAN:
Take back the lands they stole from you.

215
00:21:49,475 --> 00:21:51,306
Burn every village!

216
00:21:51,602 --> 00:21:54,059
[YELLING]

217
00:21:54,522 --> 00:21:59,687
SARUMAN: <i>We have only to</i>
<i>remove those who oppose us.</i>

218
00:22:00,194 --> 00:22:02,731
<i>It will begin in Rohan.</i>

219
00:22:03,489 --> 00:22:07,073
<i>Too long have these peasants</i>
<i>stood against you.</i>

220
00:22:07,159 --> 00:22:09,070
<i>But no more.</i>

221
00:22:09,161 --> 00:22:11,402
Éothain! Éothain!

222
00:22:13,582 --> 00:22:16,244
You take your sister.
You'll go faster with just two.

223
00:22:16,627 --> 00:22:19,334
FREDA:
Papa says Éothain must not ride Garulf.

224
00:22:19,421 --> 00:22:21,161
He is too big for him.

225
00:22:21,257 --> 00:22:24,340
Listen to me. You must ride to Edoras
and raise the alarm.

226
00:22:24,426 --> 00:22:27,008
-Do you understand me?
-Yes, Mama.

227
00:22:27,263 --> 00:22:30,221
I don't want to leave.
I don't want to go, Mama.

228
00:22:30,307 --> 00:22:34,095
Freda, I will find you there.

229
00:22:34,186 --> 00:22:35,767
[SCREAMING]

230
00:22:38,983 --> 00:22:40,723
Quickly!

231
00:22:47,074 --> 00:22:48,655
Go, child.

232
00:23:01,505 --> 00:23:03,496
SARUMAN:
<i>Rohan, my lord...</i>

233
00:23:03,924 --> 00:23:06,757
<i>...is ready to fall.</i>

234
00:23:06,844 --> 00:23:09,130
[THUNDER ROLLING]

235
00:23:12,558 --> 00:23:15,015
[HOOVES BEATING]

236
00:23:17,897 --> 00:23:19,512
Théodred.

237
00:23:19,607 --> 00:23:21,268
Find the king's son!

238
00:23:37,708 --> 00:23:43,795
-Mordor will pay for this.
-These Orcs are not from Mordor.

239
00:23:44,632 --> 00:23:47,465
My Lord Éomer, over here!

240
00:23:56,310 --> 00:23:57,971
He's alive.

241
00:24:28,926 --> 00:24:31,008
Théodred.

242
00:24:44,358 --> 00:24:47,395
ÉOWYN:
Your son is badly wounded, my lord.

243
00:24:47,861 --> 00:24:50,352
He was ambushed by Orcs.

244
00:24:51,865 --> 00:24:55,483
If we don't defend our country,
Saruman will take it by force.

245
00:24:55,869 --> 00:24:58,360
That is a lie.

246
00:25:00,541 --> 00:25:05,410
Saruman the White has ever been
our friend and ally.

247
00:25:07,047 --> 00:25:09,083
THÉODEN:
Gríma.

248
00:25:10,509 --> 00:25:12,420
Gríma.

249
00:25:14,972 --> 00:25:16,508
Gríma.

250
00:25:17,266 --> 00:25:20,383
Orcs are roaming freely
across our lands.

251
00:25:20,728 --> 00:25:24,391
Unchecked. Unchallenged.
Killing at will.

252
00:25:25,024 --> 00:25:27,891
Orcs bearing the White Hand of Saruman.

253
00:25:35,743 --> 00:25:41,579
Why do you lay these troubles
on an already troubled mind?

254
00:25:41,665 --> 00:25:44,202
Can you not see?

255
00:25:44,293 --> 00:25:49,413
Your uncle is wearied
by your malcontent...

256
00:25:49,506 --> 00:25:52,088
...your warmongering.

257
00:25:54,303 --> 00:25:56,294
Warmongering?

258
00:25:56,388 --> 00:25:58,595
How long is it since
Saruman bought you?

259
00:25:59,433 --> 00:26:01,799
What was the promised price, Gríma?

260
00:26:02,061 --> 00:26:05,724
When all the Men are dead,
you will take your share of the treasure?

261
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:20,867
Too long have you watched my sister.

262
00:26:20,954 --> 00:26:22,990
Too long have you haunted her steps.

263
00:26:31,048 --> 00:26:35,417
You see much, Éomer, son of Éomund.

264
00:26:35,511 --> 00:26:36,717
Too much.

265
00:26:37,221 --> 00:26:38,927
[GRUNTING]

266
00:26:39,014 --> 00:26:43,883
You are banished forthwith
from the kingdom of Rohan...

267
00:26:43,977 --> 00:26:48,812
...and all its domains
under pain of death.

268
00:26:49,274 --> 00:26:51,640
You have no authority here.

269
00:26:51,735 --> 00:26:54,226
Your orders mean nothing.

270
00:26:54,780 --> 00:26:58,648
This order does not come from me.

271
00:26:58,742 --> 00:27:00,983
It comes from the king.

272
00:27:01,537 --> 00:27:04,199
He signed it this morning.

273
00:27:07,126 --> 00:27:08,787
[YELLS]

274
00:27:35,737 --> 00:27:38,524
Keep breathing. That's the key.

275
00:27:38,615 --> 00:27:40,355
Breathe.

276
00:27:44,538 --> 00:27:48,326
They've run as if the very whips
of their masters were behind them.

277
00:28:04,558 --> 00:28:06,549
ORC 1:
We're not going no further...

278
00:28:06,643 --> 00:28:08,679
...until we've had a breather.

279
00:28:09,229 --> 00:28:11,185
Get a fire going!

280
00:28:15,277 --> 00:28:16,858
Merry!

281
00:28:17,196 --> 00:28:18,561
Merry!

282
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:25,451
I think we might have made a mistake
leaving the Shire, Pippin.

283
00:28:30,751 --> 00:28:33,788
[GROANING]

284
00:28:34,880 --> 00:28:37,087
What's making that noise?

285
00:28:38,675 --> 00:28:40,131
It's the trees.

286
00:28:40,886 --> 00:28:41,921
What?

287
00:28:42,262 --> 00:28:46,130
You remember the Old Forest,
on the borders of Buckland?

288
00:28:46,225 --> 00:28:50,810
Folk used to say there was something in
the water that made the trees grow tall...

289
00:28:50,896 --> 00:28:52,477
...and come alive.

290
00:28:52,731 --> 00:28:54,392
Alive?

291
00:28:55,275 --> 00:28:56,981
Trees that could whisper...

292
00:28:57,986 --> 00:29:00,477
...talk to each other...

293
00:29:00,572 --> 00:29:02,483
...even move.

294
00:29:04,117 --> 00:29:06,358
I'm starving.

295
00:29:06,453 --> 00:29:10,571
We ain't had nothing but maggoty bread
for three stinking days.

296
00:29:10,916 --> 00:29:12,281
Yeah!

297
00:29:12,376 --> 00:29:15,664
Why can't we have some meat?!

298
00:29:18,048 --> 00:29:20,289
What about them?

299
00:29:20,384 --> 00:29:22,295
They're fresh.

300
00:29:22,970 --> 00:29:26,758
They are not for eating.

301
00:29:32,729 --> 00:29:34,720
What about their legs?

302
00:29:34,815 --> 00:29:37,181
They don't need those.

303
00:29:38,652 --> 00:29:41,815
-They look tasty.
LEADER: Get back, scum!

304
00:29:43,657 --> 00:29:48,526
The prisoners go to Saruman.
Alive and unspoiled.

305
00:29:48,912 --> 00:29:50,823
Alive?

306
00:29:53,792 --> 00:29:58,081
Why alive?
Do they give good sport?

307
00:30:00,465 --> 00:30:03,878
They have something.
An Elvish weapon.

308
00:30:03,969 --> 00:30:07,052
The master wants it for the war.

309
00:30:09,933 --> 00:30:11,844
-They think we have the Ring.
-Shh.

310
00:30:11,935 --> 00:30:14,392
As soon as they find out we don't,
we're dead.

311
00:30:16,273 --> 00:30:18,264
Just a mouthful...

312
00:30:18,358 --> 00:30:19,598
...a bit of the flank.

313
00:30:26,408 --> 00:30:30,071
Looks like meat's back on the menu,
boys.

314
00:30:30,162 --> 00:30:32,118
[ROARING]

315
00:30:36,585 --> 00:30:37,870
Pippin.

316
00:30:37,961 --> 00:30:39,701
Let's go.

317
00:30:48,138 --> 00:30:49,719
Go on.

318
00:30:49,806 --> 00:30:51,342
Call for help.

319
00:30:52,726 --> 00:30:53,886
Squeal.

320
00:30:53,977 --> 00:30:57,219
No one's going to save you now.

321
00:31:01,234 --> 00:31:02,770
[HORSES NEIGHING]

322
00:31:06,406 --> 00:31:07,816
MERRY:
Pippin!

323
00:31:32,057 --> 00:31:34,548
A red sun rises.

324
00:31:35,060 --> 00:31:37,972
Blood has been spilled this night.

325
00:31:50,450 --> 00:31:52,907
[HOOVES BEATING]

326
00:32:09,219 --> 00:32:11,084
Riders of Rohan...

327
00:32:11,513 --> 00:32:13,925
...what news from the Mark?

328
00:32:41,668 --> 00:32:46,082
What business does an Elf, a Man
and a Dwarf have in the Riddermark?

329
00:32:46,882 --> 00:32:48,122
Speak quickly!

330
00:32:48,467 --> 00:32:53,131
Give me your name, horse-master,
and I shall give you mine.

331
00:33:02,272 --> 00:33:04,854
I would cut off your head, Dwarf...

332
00:33:05,358 --> 00:33:07,644
...if it stood but a little higher
from the ground.

333
00:33:08,695 --> 00:33:10,777
You would die before your stroke fell.

334
00:33:19,498 --> 00:33:21,363
I am Aragorn, son of Arathorn.

335
00:33:21,708 --> 00:33:25,951
This is Gimli, son of Glóin,
and Legolas of the Woodland Realm.

336
00:33:26,046 --> 00:33:29,379
We are friends of Rohan
and of Théoden, your king.

337
00:33:31,009 --> 00:33:34,877
Théoden no longer recognizes
friend from foe.

338
00:33:34,971 --> 00:33:37,212
Not even his own kin.

339
00:33:41,728 --> 00:33:43,764
Saruman has poisoned the mind
of the king...

340
00:33:43,855 --> 00:33:45,811
...and claimed lordship over these lands.

341
00:33:47,776 --> 00:33:50,813
My company are those loyal to Rohan.

342
00:33:50,904 --> 00:33:52,690
And for that, we are banished.

343
00:33:54,783 --> 00:33:58,071
The White Wizard is cunning.

344
00:33:58,745 --> 00:34:01,202
He walks here and there, they say...

345
00:34:01,289 --> 00:34:03,405
...as an old man hooded and cloaked.

346
00:34:05,252 --> 00:34:09,086
And everywhere, his spies
slip past our nets.

347
00:34:09,172 --> 00:34:11,458
We are no spies.

348
00:34:11,550 --> 00:34:14,542
We track a party of Uruk-hai
westward across the plain.

349
00:34:14,844 --> 00:34:17,176
They have taken two of our friends
captive.

350
00:34:17,973 --> 00:34:20,464
The Uruks are destroyed.
We slaughtered them during the night.

351
00:34:20,559 --> 00:34:23,801
But there were two Hobbits.
Did you see two Hobbits with them?

352
00:34:23,895 --> 00:34:26,932
They would be small.
Only children to your eyes.

353
00:34:30,235 --> 00:34:32,226
We left none alive.

354
00:34:32,946 --> 00:34:35,813
We piled the carcasses and burned them.

355
00:34:41,288 --> 00:34:42,528
Dead?

356
00:34:45,542 --> 00:34:47,248
I am sorry.

357
00:34:51,590 --> 00:34:52,670
[WHISTLES]

358
00:34:52,757 --> 00:34:55,089
Hasufel! Arod!

359
00:34:56,970 --> 00:35:01,589
May these horses bear you to better
fortune than their former masters.

360
00:35:02,851 --> 00:35:04,466
Farewell.

361
00:35:09,608 --> 00:35:11,894
Look for your friends.

362
00:35:12,319 --> 00:35:14,560
But do not trust to hope.

363
00:35:16,281 --> 00:35:18,897
It has forsaken these lands.

364
00:35:18,992 --> 00:35:21,028
We ride north!

365
00:36:11,670 --> 00:36:13,535
It's one of their wee belts.

366
00:36:14,547 --> 00:36:16,959
[IN ELVISH]

367
00:36:21,680 --> 00:36:23,466
[YELLS]

368
00:36:27,268 --> 00:36:29,304
We failed them.

369
00:36:43,368 --> 00:36:45,575
A Hobbit lay here.

370
00:36:47,414 --> 00:36:49,075
And the other.

371
00:36:59,843 --> 00:37:01,424
They crawled.

372
00:37:05,598 --> 00:37:07,714
Their hands were bound.

373
00:37:19,863 --> 00:37:21,694
Their bonds were cut.

374
00:37:37,130 --> 00:37:39,246
They ran over here.

375
00:37:42,927 --> 00:37:44,133
They were followed.

376
00:37:47,307 --> 00:37:49,047
MERRY:
The belt!

377
00:37:52,937 --> 00:37:54,143
Run!

378
00:37:57,776 --> 00:37:59,141
Tracks lead away from the battle...

379
00:38:03,990 --> 00:38:06,151
...into Fangorn Forest.

380
00:38:06,993 --> 00:38:08,529
Fangorn?

381
00:38:08,620 --> 00:38:11,236
What madness drove them in there?

382
00:38:27,514 --> 00:38:28,845
[TREES GROANING]

383
00:38:28,932 --> 00:38:31,969
PIPPIN:
Did we lose him? I think we lost him.

384
00:38:32,310 --> 00:38:35,017
[SNARLING]

385
00:38:38,691 --> 00:38:42,104
I'm going to rip out
your filthy little innards!

386
00:38:48,284 --> 00:38:49,319
Come here!

387
00:38:54,833 --> 00:38:57,415
Trees. Climb a tree.

388
00:39:06,761 --> 00:39:08,501
He's gone.

389
00:39:09,138 --> 00:39:10,344
[GROWLING]

390
00:39:20,567 --> 00:39:22,899
Merry!

391
00:39:24,320 --> 00:39:27,312
[GROANS]

392
00:39:34,372 --> 00:39:38,741
Let's put a maggot hole in your belly!

393
00:39:45,884 --> 00:39:47,420
Run, Merry!

394
00:39:53,766 --> 00:39:55,552
[HOBBITS GRUNTING]

395
00:39:57,270 --> 00:40:01,639
Little Orcs.

396
00:40:01,733 --> 00:40:04,145
It's talking, Merry.
The tree is talking.

397
00:40:04,235 --> 00:40:06,146
Tree?

398
00:40:06,237 --> 00:40:09,354
I am no tree!

399
00:40:09,449 --> 00:40:11,690
I am an Ent.

400
00:40:12,285 --> 00:40:14,401
A tree-herder.

401
00:40:14,913 --> 00:40:16,949
A shepherd of the forest.

402
00:40:17,040 --> 00:40:18,405
Don't talk to it, Merry.

403
00:40:18,917 --> 00:40:20,453
Don't encourage it!

404
00:40:20,543 --> 00:40:24,877
Treebeard, some call me.

405
00:40:24,964 --> 00:40:26,955
And whose side are you on?

406
00:40:27,592 --> 00:40:29,298
Side?

407
00:40:29,385 --> 00:40:32,297
I am on nobody's side...

408
00:40:32,639 --> 00:40:37,975
...because nobody's on my side,
little Orc.

409
00:40:38,811 --> 00:40:43,430
Nobody cares for the woods anymore.

410
00:40:43,816 --> 00:40:46,228
We're not Orcs! We're Hobbits!

411
00:40:46,319 --> 00:40:48,651
Hobbits?

412
00:40:49,906 --> 00:40:54,821
Never heard of a Hobbit before.

413
00:40:55,954 --> 00:40:59,287
Sounds like Orc mischief to me!

414
00:40:59,374 --> 00:41:00,489
[HOBBITS GROANING]

415
00:41:00,583 --> 00:41:02,915
They come with fire.

416
00:41:03,002 --> 00:41:05,709
They come with axes.

417
00:41:05,797 --> 00:41:10,712
Gnawing, biting, breaking,
hacking, burning!

418
00:41:10,802 --> 00:41:14,715
-Destroyers and usurpers! Curse them!
-No!

419
00:41:14,806 --> 00:41:17,718
You don't understand. We're Hobbits!

420
00:41:17,809 --> 00:41:19,720
Halflings!

421
00:41:19,811 --> 00:41:21,017
Shire-folk!

422
00:41:21,104 --> 00:41:23,470
Maybe you are...

423
00:41:23,773 --> 00:41:27,391
...and maybe you aren't.

424
00:41:28,486 --> 00:41:32,399
The White Wizard will know.

425
00:41:33,199 --> 00:41:35,155
The White Wizard?

426
00:41:36,661 --> 00:41:38,151
Saruman.

427
00:41:50,717 --> 00:41:52,503
GOLLUM:
See? See?

428
00:41:52,593 --> 00:41:55,050
We've led you out.

429
00:41:55,138 --> 00:41:57,720
Hurry, Hobbitses. Hurry!

430
00:42:00,810 --> 00:42:03,392
Very lucky we find you.

431
00:42:10,028 --> 00:42:11,734
Nice Hobbit.

432
00:42:13,406 --> 00:42:17,945
Oh! It's a bog. He's led us into a swamp.

433
00:42:18,036 --> 00:42:20,698
A swamp, yes, yes.

434
00:42:21,456 --> 00:42:26,200
Come, master. We will take you
on safe paths through the mist.

435
00:42:28,504 --> 00:42:31,962
Come, Hobbits! Come! We go quickly.

436
00:42:35,219 --> 00:42:37,926
I found it. I did.

437
00:42:38,014 --> 00:42:40,801
The way through the marshes.

438
00:42:40,892 --> 00:42:44,476
Orcs don't use it.
Orcs don't know it.

439
00:42:44,562 --> 00:42:48,680
They go around for miles and miles.

440
00:42:48,941 --> 00:42:50,397
Come quickly.

441
00:42:50,485 --> 00:42:54,569
Soft and quick as shadows we must be.

442
00:42:55,740 --> 00:42:59,107
I hate this place. It's too quiet.

443
00:42:59,202 --> 00:43:01,534
There's been no sight nor sound
of a bird for two days.

444
00:43:01,621 --> 00:43:05,079
No, no birdses to eat.

445
00:43:05,333 --> 00:43:09,576
No crunchable birdses.

446
00:43:10,171 --> 00:43:13,083
And we are famished! Yes!

447
00:43:13,174 --> 00:43:17,508
Famished we are, precious!

448
00:43:32,485 --> 00:43:33,975
Here.

449
00:43:35,154 --> 00:43:37,236
GOLLUM:
What does it eats?

450
00:43:37,323 --> 00:43:39,314
Is it tasty?

451
00:43:41,828 --> 00:43:43,693
[COUGHS]

452
00:43:44,622 --> 00:43:47,238
It tries to chokes us!

453
00:43:47,500 --> 00:43:51,163
We can't eats Hobbit food!

454
00:43:52,880 --> 00:43:56,964
We must starve!

455
00:43:57,051 --> 00:43:59,508
Well, starve, then. And good riddance!

456
00:44:00,221 --> 00:44:02,507
Oh, cruel Hobbit.

457
00:44:02,598 --> 00:44:05,590
It does not care if we be hungry.

458
00:44:05,685 --> 00:44:10,520
Does not care if we should die.

459
00:44:11,107 --> 00:44:13,940
Not like master.

460
00:44:15,319 --> 00:44:17,401
Master cares.

461
00:44:18,573 --> 00:44:20,438
Master knows.

462
00:44:22,910 --> 00:44:24,901
Yes.

463
00:44:24,996 --> 00:44:27,658
Precious.

464
00:44:31,252 --> 00:44:34,870
Once it takes hold of us...

465
00:44:36,716 --> 00:44:40,925
...it never lets go.

466
00:44:41,596 --> 00:44:42,756
Don't touch me!

467
00:45:15,254 --> 00:45:17,165
SAM:
There are dead things!

468
00:45:17,256 --> 00:45:19,087
Dead faces in the water.

469
00:45:23,888 --> 00:45:27,881
GOLLUM:
All dead. All rotten.

470
00:45:28,392 --> 00:45:32,226
Elves and Men and Orcses.

471
00:45:32,313 --> 00:45:35,976
A great battle long ago.

472
00:45:36,776 --> 00:45:38,607
Dead Marshes.

473
00:45:38,694 --> 00:45:41,436
Yes. Yes, that is their name.

474
00:45:43,115 --> 00:45:44,980
This way.

475
00:45:45,076 --> 00:45:47,818
Don't follow the lights.

476
00:45:49,622 --> 00:45:53,490
Careful now! Or Hobbits go down
to join the dead ones...

477
00:45:53,584 --> 00:45:57,748
...and light little candles
of their own.

478
00:46:23,948 --> 00:46:25,438
Frodo!

479
00:47:02,611 --> 00:47:05,273
[FRODO GASPS]

480
00:47:09,952 --> 00:47:14,662
-Gollum?
-Don't follow the lights.

481
00:47:14,749 --> 00:47:16,580
FRODO: Gollum!
-Mr. Frodo!

482
00:47:16,834 --> 00:47:18,699
Are you all right?

483
00:47:22,089 --> 00:47:24,751
[THUNDER ROLLING]

484
00:47:47,531 --> 00:47:50,614
GOLLUM:
So bright.

485
00:47:50,701 --> 00:47:54,614
So beautiful.

486
00:47:54,705 --> 00:47:58,539
Our precious.

487
00:48:00,002 --> 00:48:01,458
What did you say?

488
00:48:01,754 --> 00:48:03,961
Master should be resting.

489
00:48:04,048 --> 00:48:08,166
Master needs to keep up his strength.

490
00:48:10,137 --> 00:48:13,425
-Who are you?
-Mustn't ask us. Not its business.

491
00:48:13,516 --> 00:48:15,097
Gollum. Gollum.

492
00:48:15,184 --> 00:48:17,140
Gandalf told me you were
one of the river-folk.

493
00:48:17,228 --> 00:48:21,346
<i>Cold be heart and hand and bone</i>
<i>Cold be travelers far from home</i>

494
00:48:21,440 --> 00:48:23,146
He said your life was a sad story.

495
00:48:23,234 --> 00:48:27,819
<i>They do not see what lies ahead</i>
<i>When sun has failed and moon is dead</i>

496
00:48:27,905 --> 00:48:30,988
You were not so very different
from a Hobbit once.

497
00:48:31,075 --> 00:48:32,906
Were you?

498
00:48:35,079 --> 00:48:37,320
Sméagol.

499
00:48:42,044 --> 00:48:44,581
What did you call me?

500
00:48:45,923 --> 00:48:48,665
That was your name once, wasn't it?

501
00:48:49,301 --> 00:48:51,587
A long time ago.

502
00:48:52,430 --> 00:48:54,591
My name.

503
00:48:55,683 --> 00:48:57,173
My name.

504
00:49:04,108 --> 00:49:06,599
Sméagol.

505
00:49:07,236 --> 00:49:09,101
[RINGWRAITH SCREECHING]

506
00:49:10,698 --> 00:49:12,359
Black Riders!

507
00:49:12,450 --> 00:49:13,860
Hide! Hide!

508
00:49:13,951 --> 00:49:16,363
[FRODO GROANING]

509
00:49:24,420 --> 00:49:26,752
Come on, Frodo. Come on!

510
00:49:26,839 --> 00:49:30,502
SMÉAGOL: Quick! They will see us!
They will see us!

511
00:49:31,343 --> 00:49:34,005
-I thought they were dead.
-Dead?

512
00:49:34,096 --> 00:49:37,054
No, you cannot kill them. No.

513
00:49:53,365 --> 00:49:55,526
[ROARS]

514
00:50:04,210 --> 00:50:05,370
SMÉAGOL:
Wraiths!

515
00:50:05,461 --> 00:50:07,702
Wraiths on wings!

516
00:50:10,633 --> 00:50:13,249
[SCREECHING]

517
00:50:15,679 --> 00:50:17,840
They are calling for it.

518
00:50:17,932 --> 00:50:21,424
They are calling for the precious.

519
00:50:23,646 --> 00:50:25,807
Mr. Frodo! It's all right.

520
00:50:25,898 --> 00:50:27,183
I'm here.

521
00:50:34,907 --> 00:50:37,068
[ROARS]

522
00:50:43,207 --> 00:50:44,743
SMÉAGOL:
Hurry, Hobbits.

523
00:50:45,292 --> 00:50:49,205
The Black Gate is very close.

524
00:50:54,927 --> 00:50:55,962
[SPITS]

525
00:50:56,053 --> 00:50:57,964
Orc blood.

526
00:51:07,982 --> 00:51:09,722
These are strange tracks.

527
00:51:11,026 --> 00:51:12,982
The air is so close in here.

528
00:51:14,196 --> 00:51:16,608
This forest is old.

529
00:51:17,449 --> 00:51:19,440
Very old.

530
00:51:21,161 --> 00:51:23,447
Full of memory...

531
00:51:26,083 --> 00:51:28,449
...and anger.

532
00:51:29,003 --> 00:51:32,086
[TREES GROANING]

533
00:51:34,592 --> 00:51:37,504
The trees are speaking to each other.

534
00:51:37,595 --> 00:51:39,176
ARAGORN:
Gimli!

535
00:51:39,263 --> 00:51:41,254
Lower your ax.

536
00:51:44,059 --> 00:51:46,801
They have feelings, my friend.

537
00:51:47,354 --> 00:51:49,390
The Elves began it.

538
00:51:49,481 --> 00:51:54,271
Waking up the trees,
teaching them to speak.

539
00:51:54,778 --> 00:51:57,110
Talking trees.

540
00:51:57,781 --> 00:52:00,864
What do trees have to talk about?

541
00:52:00,951 --> 00:52:04,193
Except the consistency
of squirrel droppings.

542
00:52:07,791 --> 00:52:09,247
[IN ELVISH]

543
00:52:15,799 --> 00:52:17,585
[IN ELVISH]

544
00:52:18,135 --> 00:52:20,592
[IN ENGLISH]
The White Wizard approaches.

545
00:52:26,769 --> 00:52:31,058
[IN ENGLISH] Do not let him speak.
He will put a spell on us.

546
00:52:40,658 --> 00:52:42,899
We must be quick.

547
00:52:58,467 --> 00:53:02,130
WHITE WIZARD: You are tracking
the footsteps of two young Hobbits.

548
00:53:02,721 --> 00:53:04,177
Where are they?

549
00:53:04,264 --> 00:53:07,927
WHITE WIZARD: They passed this way
the day before yesterday.

550
00:53:08,018 --> 00:53:12,352
They met someone they did not expect.

551
00:53:12,439 --> 00:53:14,646
Does that comfort you?

552
00:53:14,733 --> 00:53:16,724
Who are you?

553
00:53:18,195 --> 00:53:20,186
Show yourself!

554
00:53:29,081 --> 00:53:31,072
It cannot be.

555
00:53:34,002 --> 00:53:35,082
Forgive me.

556
00:53:36,672 --> 00:53:38,583
I mistook you for Saruman.

557
00:53:39,383 --> 00:53:42,125
I am Saruman.

558
00:53:43,679 --> 00:53:47,592
Or rather, Saruman
as he should have been.

559
00:53:48,517 --> 00:53:50,007
You fell.

560
00:53:51,478 --> 00:53:54,060
Through fire...

561
00:53:54,148 --> 00:53:55,479
...and water.

562
00:53:56,942 --> 00:53:59,524
<i>From the lowest dungeon</i>
<i>to the highest peak...</i>

563
00:53:59,611 --> 00:54:03,399
<i>...I fought with the Balrog</i>
<i>of Morgoth.</i>

564
00:54:04,158 --> 00:54:06,524
[ROARING AND YELLING]

565
00:54:19,256 --> 00:54:21,998
GANDALF: <i>Until at last</i>
<i>I threw down my enemy...</i>

566
00:54:22,092 --> 00:54:26,631
<i>...and smote his ruin</i>
<i>upon the mountainside.</i>

567
00:54:32,644 --> 00:54:35,181
<i>Darkness took me...</i>

568
00:54:35,939 --> 00:54:40,023
<i>...and I strayed out of thought</i>
<i>and time.</i>

569
00:54:40,778 --> 00:54:43,861
<i>Stars wheeled overhead...</i>

570
00:54:44,156 --> 00:54:48,650
<i>...and every day was as long</i>
<i>as a life age of the Earth.</i>

571
00:54:50,746 --> 00:54:52,862
<i>But it was not the end.</i>

572
00:54:53,165 --> 00:54:55,952
<i>I felt life in me again.</i>

573
00:54:57,878 --> 00:55:00,460
<i>I've been sent back...</i>

574
00:55:00,547 --> 00:55:02,162
...until my task is done.

575
00:55:02,591 --> 00:55:04,456
Gandalf.

576
00:55:05,177 --> 00:55:07,168
Gandalf?

577
00:55:07,554 --> 00:55:09,340
Yes.

578
00:55:12,184 --> 00:55:13,924
That was what they used to call me.

579
00:55:16,814 --> 00:55:19,055
Gandalf the Grey.

580
00:55:20,400 --> 00:55:22,265
That was my name.

581
00:55:22,361 --> 00:55:23,771
Gandalf.

582
00:55:25,739 --> 00:55:27,821
I am Gandalf the White.

583
00:55:30,828 --> 00:55:33,945
And I come back to you now...

584
00:55:34,039 --> 00:55:36,576
...at the turn of the tide.

585
00:55:37,709 --> 00:55:40,701
One stage of your journey is over.
Another begins.

586
00:55:41,421 --> 00:55:44,584
-We must travel to Edoras with all speed.
GIMLI: Edoras?

587
00:55:45,509 --> 00:55:47,545
That is no short distance!

588
00:55:47,803 --> 00:55:51,091
We hear of trouble in Rohan.
It goes ill with the king.

589
00:55:51,181 --> 00:55:53,342
Yes, and it will not be easily cured.

590
00:55:53,433 --> 00:55:56,925
Then we have run all this way for nothing?

591
00:55:57,020 --> 00:55:59,102
Are we to leave those poor Hobbits here...

592
00:55:59,189 --> 00:56:03,182
...in this horrid, dark, dank,
tree-infested--?

593
00:56:03,277 --> 00:56:05,643
[TREES GROANING]

594
00:56:06,071 --> 00:56:09,279
I mean, charming...

595
00:56:09,366 --> 00:56:12,153
...quite charming forest.

596
00:56:12,744 --> 00:56:16,407
It was more than mere chance that
brought Merry and Pippin to Fangorn.

597
00:56:16,498 --> 00:56:20,912
A great power has been sleeping here
for many long years.

598
00:56:21,003 --> 00:56:24,541
The coming of Merry and Pippin
will be like the falling of small stones...

599
00:56:24,631 --> 00:56:28,044
...that starts an avalanche
in the mountains.

600
00:56:28,135 --> 00:56:30,376
In one thing you have not changed,
dear friend.

601
00:56:30,470 --> 00:56:34,930
-Hm?
-You still speak in riddles.

602
00:56:37,769 --> 00:56:44,231
A thing is about to happen that has not
happened since the Elder Days.

603
00:56:44,318 --> 00:56:47,981
The Ents are going to wake up...

604
00:56:48,530 --> 00:56:53,024
-...and find that they are strong.
-Strong?!

605
00:56:53,785 --> 00:56:54,991
Oh, that's good.

606
00:56:55,078 --> 00:56:57,820
So stop your fretting, Master Dwarf.

607
00:56:58,916 --> 00:57:01,202
Merry and Pippin are quite safe.

608
00:57:01,293 --> 00:57:05,036
In fact, they are far safer
than you are about to be.

609
00:57:05,130 --> 00:57:08,918
This new Gandalf's more grumpy
than the old one.

610
00:57:09,176 --> 00:57:11,212
[WHISTLING]

611
00:57:20,604 --> 00:57:22,435
[HORSE NEIGHS]

612
00:57:31,156 --> 00:57:32,692
That is one of the Mearas...

613
00:57:32,783 --> 00:57:35,570
...unless my eyes are cheated
by some spell.

614
00:57:53,178 --> 00:57:55,464
GANDALF:
Shadowfax.

615
00:57:58,058 --> 00:58:00,640
He is the lord of all horses...

616
00:58:02,270 --> 00:58:06,183
...and has been my friend
through many dangers.

617
00:58:20,455 --> 00:58:24,073
TREEBEARD:
<i>O rowan mine</i>

618
00:58:24,167 --> 00:58:28,035
<i>I saw you shine</i>

619
00:58:28,130 --> 00:58:31,714
<i>Upon a summer's day</i>

620
00:58:32,801 --> 00:58:37,340
<i>Upon your head</i>
<i>How golden-red</i>

621
00:58:37,431 --> 00:58:42,266
<i>The crown you bore aloft</i>

622
00:58:42,352 --> 00:58:44,809
Such a beautiful verse.

623
00:58:44,896 --> 00:58:49,890
-Is it much further?
-Bru-ra-hroom. Don't be hasty.

624
00:58:49,985 --> 00:58:53,273
You might call it far, perhaps.

625
00:58:54,197 --> 00:58:58,065
My home lies deep in the forest...

626
00:58:58,160 --> 00:59:02,073
...near the roots of the mountain.

627
00:59:03,415 --> 00:59:07,158
I told Gandalf I would keep you safe.

628
00:59:07,252 --> 00:59:11,291
And safe is where I'll keep you.

629
00:59:11,548 --> 00:59:15,917
I believe you will enjoy this next one too.

630
00:59:16,303 --> 00:59:19,340
It's one of my own compositions.

631
00:59:19,431 --> 00:59:20,716
Right.

632
00:59:20,807 --> 00:59:27,019
<i>Beneath the roof of sleeping leaves</i>

633
00:59:27,105 --> 00:59:32,065
<i>And the dreams of trees unfold</i>

634
00:59:32,152 --> 00:59:38,694
<i>When woodland halls are green and cool</i>

635
00:59:38,784 --> 00:59:42,948
<i>And the wind is in the West</i>

636
00:59:43,371 --> 00:59:46,033
<i>Come back to me</i>

637
00:59:46,583 --> 00:59:51,077
<i>Come back to me</i>

638
00:59:51,171 --> 00:59:57,633
<i>And say my land is best</i>

639
00:59:59,137 --> 01:00:01,093
Oh.

640
01:00:05,102 --> 01:00:08,845
Sleep, little Shirelings.

641
01:00:08,939 --> 01:00:12,557
Heed no nightly noise.

642
01:00:12,651 --> 01:00:16,610
Sleep till morning light.

643
01:00:18,240 --> 01:00:22,449
I have business in the forest.

644
01:00:22,536 --> 01:00:28,122
There are many to call.
Many that must come.

645
01:00:29,334 --> 01:00:34,044
The Shadow lies on Fangorn.

646
01:00:34,131 --> 01:00:39,876
The withering of all woods
is drawing near.

647
01:00:49,437 --> 01:00:53,680
The veiling shadow that glowers
in the east takes shape.

648
01:00:54,526 --> 01:00:57,108
Sauron will suffer no rival.

649
01:00:57,529 --> 01:01:01,898
From the summit of Barad-dûr,
his Eye watches ceaselessly.

650
01:01:01,992 --> 01:01:05,405
But he is not so mighty yet
that he is above fear.

651
01:01:06,454 --> 01:01:08,445
Doubt ever gnaws at him.

652
01:01:08,540 --> 01:01:11,202
The rumor has reached him.

653
01:01:11,293 --> 01:01:14,285
The heir of Númenor still lives.

654
01:01:15,255 --> 01:01:18,088
Sauron fears you, Aragorn.

655
01:01:19,384 --> 01:01:21,591
He fears what you may become.

656
01:01:22,846 --> 01:01:26,304
And so he'll strike hard and fast
at the world of Men.

657
01:01:26,391 --> 01:01:30,100
He will use his puppet, Saruman,
to destroy Rohan.

658
01:01:30,187 --> 01:01:31,768
War is coming.

659
01:01:31,855 --> 01:01:35,518
Rohan must defend itself,
and therein lies our first challenge...

660
01:01:35,609 --> 01:01:38,100
...for Rohan is weak and ready to fall.

661
01:01:38,195 --> 01:01:41,983
The king's mind is enslaved,
it's an old device of Saruman's.

662
01:01:42,073 --> 01:01:45,236
His hold over King Théoden
is now very strong.

663
01:01:45,327 --> 01:01:50,071
Sauron and Saruman
are tightening the noose.

664
01:01:50,874 --> 01:01:53,081
But for all their cunning...

665
01:01:53,168 --> 01:01:55,784
...we have one advantage.

666
01:01:57,923 --> 01:02:00,505
The Ring remains hidden.

667
01:02:01,593 --> 01:02:03,549
And that we should seek to destroy it...

668
01:02:03,637 --> 01:02:06,629
...has not yet entered
their darkest dreams.

669
01:02:07,224 --> 01:02:10,591
And so the weapon of the enemy
is moving towards Mordor...

670
01:02:10,685 --> 01:02:12,266
...in the hands of a Hobbit.

671
01:02:12,354 --> 01:02:16,518
Each day brings it closer
to the fires of Mount Doom.

672
01:02:16,608 --> 01:02:19,315
We must trust now in Frodo.

673
01:02:19,402 --> 01:02:21,313
Everything depends upon speed...

674
01:02:21,404 --> 01:02:24,441
...and the secrecy of his quest.

675
01:02:26,409 --> 01:02:29,742
Do not regret your decision to leave him.

676
01:02:30,622 --> 01:02:33,364
Frodo must finish this task alone.

677
01:02:34,125 --> 01:02:36,491
He's not alone.

678
01:02:36,586 --> 01:02:38,292
Sam went with him.

679
01:02:38,964 --> 01:02:40,204
Did he?

680
01:02:40,298 --> 01:02:44,962
Did he, indeed? Good.

681
01:02:45,637 --> 01:02:48,003
Yes, very good.

682
01:02:56,022 --> 01:03:00,891
SMÉAGOL:
The Black Gate of Mordor.

683
01:03:03,697 --> 01:03:06,188
Oh, save us.

684
01:03:11,955 --> 01:03:15,197
My old Gaffer would have a thing or two
to say if he could see us now.

685
01:03:17,460 --> 01:03:21,954
SMÉAGOL: Master says to
show him the way into Mordor.

686
01:03:22,048 --> 01:03:25,540
So good Sméagol does,
master says so.

687
01:03:25,635 --> 01:03:26,920
I did.

688
01:03:35,687 --> 01:03:37,678
That's it, then.

689
01:03:39,232 --> 01:03:40,517
We can't get past that.

690
01:03:41,067 --> 01:03:43,979
[EASTERLINGS YELLING
INDISTINCTLY]

691
01:03:51,703 --> 01:03:54,285
[HORNS BLOWING]

692
01:04:04,341 --> 01:04:06,377
[ROARS]

693
01:04:25,737 --> 01:04:27,102
Look!

694
01:04:27,197 --> 01:04:28,733
The gate.

695
01:04:28,823 --> 01:04:30,063
It's opening!

696
01:04:37,499 --> 01:04:39,490
I can see a way down.

697
01:04:40,251 --> 01:04:42,333
Sam, no!

698
01:04:44,506 --> 01:04:45,871
Master!

699
01:06:02,459 --> 01:06:05,166
[EASTERLINGS YELLING
INDISTINCTLY]

700
01:06:09,716 --> 01:06:13,254
-I do not ask you to come with me, Sam.
-I know, Mr. Frodo.

701
01:06:14,012 --> 01:06:17,175
I doubt even these Elvish cloaks
will hide us in there.

702
01:06:17,599 --> 01:06:19,464
-Now!
SMÉAGOL: No!

703
01:06:20,018 --> 01:06:21,929
No! No, master!

704
01:06:22,187 --> 01:06:25,179
They catch you! They catch you!

705
01:06:26,483 --> 01:06:29,020
Don't take it to him.

706
01:06:31,988 --> 01:06:34,730
He wants the precious.

707
01:06:34,824 --> 01:06:37,941
Always he is looking for it.

708
01:06:38,036 --> 01:06:42,075
And the precious is wanting
to go back to him.

709
01:06:42,165 --> 01:06:46,124
But we mustn't let him have it.

710
01:06:52,509 --> 01:06:54,670
No! There's another way.

711
01:06:54,761 --> 01:06:57,468
More secret. A dark way.

712
01:06:57,764 --> 01:07:01,427
-Why haven't you spoken of this before?
-Because master did not ask.

713
01:07:01,893 --> 01:07:03,008
He's up to something.

714
01:07:03,603 --> 01:07:06,265
Are you saying there's another way
into Mordor?

715
01:07:06,356 --> 01:07:09,143
Yes. There's a path...

716
01:07:09,234 --> 01:07:11,850
...and some stairs.

717
01:07:11,945 --> 01:07:13,685
And then...

718
01:07:13,780 --> 01:07:17,147
...a tunnel.

719
01:07:17,534 --> 01:07:19,741
[RUMBLING]

720
01:07:31,130 --> 01:07:32,961
He's led us this far, Sam.

721
01:07:33,049 --> 01:07:34,505
Mr. Frodo, no.

722
01:07:35,635 --> 01:07:37,091
He's been true to his word.

723
01:07:41,975 --> 01:07:43,181
No.

724
01:07:45,311 --> 01:07:46,926
Lead the way, Sméagol.

725
01:07:47,564 --> 01:07:51,477
Good Sméagol always helps.

726
01:08:25,476 --> 01:08:26,465
Hello?

727
01:08:28,896 --> 01:08:30,932
Treebeard?

728
01:08:31,608 --> 01:08:33,018
Where has he gone?

729
01:08:33,109 --> 01:08:35,600
PIPPIN:
I had the loveliest dream last night.

730
01:08:36,237 --> 01:08:38,979
There was this large barrel,
full of pipe-weed.

731
01:08:39,073 --> 01:08:41,610
And we smoked all of it.
And then...

732
01:08:42,118 --> 01:08:44,029
...you were sick.

733
01:08:45,622 --> 01:08:48,489
I'd give anything for a whiff of Old Toby.

734
01:08:49,584 --> 01:08:51,666
[GROANING]

735
01:08:52,003 --> 01:08:53,914
Did you hear that?

736
01:09:01,012 --> 01:09:02,502
There it is again.

737
01:09:03,348 --> 01:09:06,966
Something's not right here.
Not right at all.

738
01:09:07,060 --> 01:09:09,221
[ENTISH GROAN]

739
01:09:11,773 --> 01:09:14,731
You just said something...Treeish.

740
01:09:14,817 --> 01:09:18,856
No, I didn't. I was just stretching.

741
01:09:26,412 --> 01:09:28,277
You're taller.

742
01:09:28,831 --> 01:09:30,412
-Who?
-You!

743
01:09:30,500 --> 01:09:32,115
-Than what?
-Than me!

744
01:09:32,627 --> 01:09:34,788
I've always been taller than you.

745
01:09:34,879 --> 01:09:39,543
Pippin, everyone knows I'm the tall one.
You're the short one.

746
01:09:40,385 --> 01:09:41,966
Please, Merry.

747
01:09:42,053 --> 01:09:45,921
You're what? Three-foot-six? At the most?

748
01:09:46,557 --> 01:09:48,718
Whereas me, I'm pushing 3'7".

749
01:09:48,810 --> 01:09:50,550
[ENTISH GROAN]

750
01:09:51,479 --> 01:09:53,720
3'8"!

751
01:09:55,692 --> 01:09:57,557
Three-foot-eight.

752
01:10:00,571 --> 01:10:02,482
You did something.

753
01:10:08,287 --> 01:10:09,868
PIPPIN:
Merry, don't! Don't drink it!

754
01:10:10,790 --> 01:10:12,326
Merry!

755
01:10:12,417 --> 01:10:14,829
No, Treebeard said that you
shouldn't have any.

756
01:10:14,919 --> 01:10:18,958
MERRY: I want some!
-It could well be dangerous!

757
01:10:19,048 --> 01:10:21,209
Give me it back. Merry!

758
01:10:23,094 --> 01:10:24,379
What's happening?!

759
01:10:25,263 --> 01:10:26,719
It's got my leg!

760
01:10:27,098 --> 01:10:28,588
Merry!

761
01:10:31,394 --> 01:10:33,885
[GRUNTING]

762
01:10:37,108 --> 01:10:38,314
No!

763
01:10:47,910 --> 01:10:49,616
PIPPIN:
Help!

764
01:10:56,294 --> 01:10:58,205
TREEBEARD:
Away with you.

765
01:10:58,296 --> 01:11:00,127
You should not be waking.

766
01:11:00,631 --> 01:11:05,625
Eat earth. Dig deep. Drink water.

767
01:11:06,179 --> 01:11:08,761
Go to sleep.

768
01:11:09,140 --> 01:11:11,005
Away with you.

769
01:11:11,100 --> 01:11:14,433
Come, the forest is waking up.

770
01:11:14,979 --> 01:11:16,935
It isn't safe.

771
01:11:19,567 --> 01:11:23,526
The trees have grown wild
and dangerous.

772
01:11:23,613 --> 01:11:26,696
Anger festers in their hearts.

773
01:11:27,533 --> 01:11:29,194
Black are their thoughts.

774
01:11:29,285 --> 01:11:31,901
Strong is their hate.

775
01:11:31,996 --> 01:11:34,829
They will harm you if they can.

776
01:11:34,916 --> 01:11:38,579
There are too few of us now.

777
01:11:38,669 --> 01:11:42,708
Too few of us Ents left to manage them.

778
01:11:43,341 --> 01:11:46,048
Why are there so few of you
when you have lived so long?

779
01:11:46,135 --> 01:11:49,377
-Are there Ent children?
-Bru-ra-hroom.

780
01:11:49,472 --> 01:11:55,183
There have been no Entings
for a terrible long count of years.

781
01:11:55,269 --> 01:12:00,559
-Why is that?
-We lost the Entwives.

782
01:12:00,817 --> 01:12:02,273
Oh, I'm sorry.

783
01:12:02,360 --> 01:12:06,353
-How did they die?
-Die? No.

784
01:12:06,447 --> 01:12:09,780
We lost them.

785
01:12:09,867 --> 01:12:15,078
And now we cannot find them.

786
01:12:15,164 --> 01:12:21,410
I don't suppose you've seen Entwives
in the Shire?

787
01:12:21,504 --> 01:12:24,120
Can't say that I have.

788
01:12:24,632 --> 01:12:26,714
You, Pip?

789
01:12:28,135 --> 01:12:30,501
What do they look like?

790
01:12:32,974 --> 01:12:37,638
I don't remember now.

791
01:12:54,036 --> 01:12:57,949
GANDALF: Edoras and the Golden Hall
of Meduseld.

792
01:12:58,749 --> 01:13:01,365
There dwells Théoden, King of Rohan...

793
01:13:02,044 --> 01:13:05,002
<i>...whose mind is overthrown.</i>

794
01:13:05,089 --> 01:13:09,378
<i>Saruman's hold over King Théoden</i>
<i>is now very strong.</i>

795
01:13:10,052 --> 01:13:13,260
ÉOWYN:
My lord, your son...

796
01:13:13,347 --> 01:13:15,554
...he is dead.

797
01:13:17,059 --> 01:13:18,890
My lord?

798
01:13:20,146 --> 01:13:21,306
Uncle?

799
01:13:28,112 --> 01:13:30,398
Will you not go to him?

800
01:13:33,492 --> 01:13:35,949
Will you do nothing?

801
01:13:36,037 --> 01:13:38,153
Be careful what you say.

802
01:13:38,247 --> 01:13:40,408
Do not look for welcome here.

803
01:14:04,482 --> 01:14:08,691
Oh, he must have died
sometime in the night.

804
01:14:08,778 --> 01:14:11,064
What a tragedy for the king...

805
01:14:11,155 --> 01:14:14,147
...to lose his only son and heir.

806
01:14:15,326 --> 01:14:19,820
I understand.
His passing is hard to accept.

807
01:14:19,914 --> 01:14:24,908
Especially now that your brother
has deserted you.

808
01:14:25,002 --> 01:14:26,492
Leave me alone, snake!

809
01:14:27,964 --> 01:14:29,625
Oh, but you are alone.

810
01:14:31,258 --> 01:14:36,048
Who knows what you've spoken
to the darkness...

811
01:14:36,138 --> 01:14:39,722
...in the bitter watches of the night...

812
01:14:39,809 --> 01:14:43,518
...when all your life seems to shrink.

813
01:14:43,604 --> 01:14:47,893
The walls of your bower
closing in about you.

814
01:14:47,984 --> 01:14:52,603
A hutch to trammel some wild thing in.

815
01:14:54,865 --> 01:14:56,730
So fair.

816
01:14:57,994 --> 01:14:59,359
So cold.

817
01:15:01,163 --> 01:15:03,449
Like a morning of pale spring...

818
01:15:03,541 --> 01:15:06,999
...still clinging to winter's chill.

819
01:15:20,766 --> 01:15:23,257
Your words are poison.

820
01:16:55,778 --> 01:16:58,269
You'll find more cheer in a graveyard.

821
01:17:11,502 --> 01:17:12,582
Ah.

822
01:17:12,670 --> 01:17:16,504
I cannot allow you before Théoden King
so armed, Gandalf Greyhame.

823
01:17:18,008 --> 01:17:20,545
By order of Gríma Wormtongue.

824
01:17:37,862 --> 01:17:40,854
-Your staff.
-Hm? Oh....

825
01:17:43,033 --> 01:17:46,525
You would not part an old man
from his walking stick.

826
01:18:05,347 --> 01:18:08,214
My lord, Gandalf the Grey is coming.

827
01:18:12,188 --> 01:18:13,974
[DOOR LOCKS]

828
01:18:16,567 --> 01:18:18,182
He's a herald of woe.

829
01:18:18,277 --> 01:18:22,691
The courtesy of your hall
is somewhat lessened of late...

830
01:18:23,824 --> 01:18:25,234
...Théoden King.

831
01:18:25,951 --> 01:18:28,488
He's not welcome.

832
01:18:29,413 --> 01:18:34,703
Why should I welcome you...

833
01:18:35,211 --> 01:18:38,954
...Gandalf Stormcrow?

834
01:18:39,048 --> 01:18:42,461
A just question, my liege.

835
01:18:42,551 --> 01:18:45,463
Late is the hour...

836
01:18:45,554 --> 01:18:49,593
...in which this conjurer
chooses to appear.

837
01:18:50,351 --> 01:18:52,467
Láthspell I name him.

838
01:18:52,561 --> 01:18:55,519
Ill news is an ill guest.

839
01:18:55,606 --> 01:19:00,270
Be silent. Keep your forked tongue
behind your teeth.

840
01:19:00,361 --> 01:19:02,352
I have not passed
through fire and death...

841
01:19:02,446 --> 01:19:05,734
...to bandy crooked words
with a witless worm.

842
01:19:06,700 --> 01:19:08,861
His staff.

843
01:19:08,953 --> 01:19:13,117
I told you to take the wizard's staff.

844
01:19:16,460 --> 01:19:18,416
Théoden...

845
01:19:18,963 --> 01:19:21,545
...son of Thengel...

846
01:19:23,300 --> 01:19:25,666
...too long have you sat
in the Shadows.

847
01:19:28,639 --> 01:19:32,006
I would stay still if I were you.

848
01:19:32,101 --> 01:19:34,183
Hearken to me!

849
01:19:39,650 --> 01:19:41,857
I release you...

850
01:19:41,944 --> 01:19:43,935
...from the spell.

851
01:19:44,571 --> 01:19:46,937
[LAUGHS]

852
01:19:55,499 --> 01:19:58,536
You have no power here...

853
01:19:58,794 --> 01:20:02,332
...Gandalf the Grey.

854
01:20:07,761 --> 01:20:12,801
I will draw you, Saruman,
as poison is drawn from a wound.

855
01:20:13,058 --> 01:20:15,299
[GROANING]

856
01:20:22,234 --> 01:20:23,770
Wait.

857
01:20:25,195 --> 01:20:29,029
SARUMAN'S VOICE:
If I go, Théoden dies.

858
01:20:29,742 --> 01:20:31,983
You did not kill me...

859
01:20:32,077 --> 01:20:34,318
...you will not kill him.

860
01:20:38,208 --> 01:20:39,914
SARUMAN:
Rohan is mine.

861
01:20:41,420 --> 01:20:42,751
Be gone.

862
01:20:47,426 --> 01:20:50,463
[YELLING]

863
01:21:00,397 --> 01:21:02,262
[GROANS]

864
01:21:27,257 --> 01:21:29,418
I know your face.

865
01:21:33,972 --> 01:21:35,257
Éowyn.

866
01:21:37,559 --> 01:21:38,799
Éowyn.

867
01:21:47,111 --> 01:21:48,271
Gandalf?

868
01:21:48,821 --> 01:21:51,688
Breathe the free air again, my friend.

869
01:22:05,087 --> 01:22:07,669
Dark have been my dreams of late.

870
01:22:11,802 --> 01:22:15,670
Your fingers would remember
their old strength better...

871
01:22:15,764 --> 01:22:18,722
...if they grasped your sword.

872
01:22:56,430 --> 01:22:58,762
[YELLS]

873
01:23:01,018 --> 01:23:02,178
[GROANS]

874
01:23:03,854 --> 01:23:05,890
WORMTONGUE:
I've only...

875
01:23:05,981 --> 01:23:09,098
...ever served you, my lord.

876
01:23:09,193 --> 01:23:14,233
Your leechcraft would have had me
crawling on all fours like a beast!

877
01:23:15,240 --> 01:23:17,196
WORMTONGUE:
Send me not from your sight.

878
01:23:19,495 --> 01:23:22,282
ARAGORN:
No, my lord! No, my lord.

879
01:23:22,372 --> 01:23:23,612
Let him go.

880
01:23:24,374 --> 01:23:27,537
Enough blood has been spilt
on his account.

881
01:23:36,678 --> 01:23:39,010
WORMTONGUE:
Get out of my way!

882
01:23:41,225 --> 01:23:44,388
MAN:
Hail, Théoden King!

883
01:24:09,044 --> 01:24:11,581
Where is Théodred?

884
01:24:14,591 --> 01:24:17,082
Where is my son?

885
01:25:05,475 --> 01:25:08,967
[CHANTING IN ROHIRRIM
ANCESTRAL LANGUAGE]

886
01:25:44,348 --> 01:25:46,054
THÉODEN:
Simbelmynë.

887
01:25:51,188 --> 01:25:54,806
Ever has it grown on the tombs
of my forebearers.

888
01:25:58,654 --> 01:26:01,612
Now it shall cover the grave
of my son.

889
01:26:03,742 --> 01:26:07,610
Alas that these evil days
should be mine.

890
01:26:08,372 --> 01:26:12,786
The young perish and the old linger.

891
01:26:13,377 --> 01:26:15,538
That I should live...

892
01:26:15,629 --> 01:26:19,042
...to see the last days of my house.

893
01:26:20,258 --> 01:26:24,126
Théodred's death
was not of your making.

894
01:26:27,182 --> 01:26:30,549
No parent should have to bury
their child.

895
01:26:47,285 --> 01:26:49,150
GANDALF:
He was strong in life.

896
01:26:50,247 --> 01:26:53,831
His spirit will find its way
to the halls of your fathers.

897
01:27:04,052 --> 01:27:06,043
[SPEAKING IN ROHIRRIM
ANCESTRAL LANGUAGE]

898
01:27:38,420 --> 01:27:40,331
They had no warning.

899
01:27:40,422 --> 01:27:42,879
They were unarmed.

900
01:27:43,341 --> 01:27:47,380
Now the Wild Men are moving through
the Westfold, burning as they go.

901
01:27:48,305 --> 01:27:50,261
Rick, cot and tree.

902
01:27:50,640 --> 01:27:52,756
-Where is Mama?
ÉOWYN: Shh.

903
01:27:53,643 --> 01:27:57,852
This is but a taste of the terror
that Saruman will unleash.

904
01:27:57,939 --> 01:28:02,399
All the more potent for he is driven now
by fear of Sauron.

905
01:28:03,987 --> 01:28:06,979
Ride out and meet him head on.

906
01:28:07,741 --> 01:28:11,233
Draw him away from your women
and children.

907
01:28:11,578 --> 01:28:13,239
You must fight.

908
01:28:13,330 --> 01:28:17,243
You have 2000 good men riding north
as we speak.

909
01:28:17,334 --> 01:28:19,040
Éomer is loyal to you.

910
01:28:19,127 --> 01:28:21,914
His men will return
and fight for their king.

911
01:28:22,005 --> 01:28:25,964
They will be 300 leagues from here
by now.

912
01:28:29,679 --> 01:28:31,840
Éomer cannot help us.

913
01:28:32,474 --> 01:28:34,305
I know what it is you want of me...

914
01:28:34,392 --> 01:28:37,680
...but I will not bring further death
to my people.

915
01:28:39,356 --> 01:28:41,062
I will not risk open war.

916
01:28:43,276 --> 01:28:46,689
Open war is upon you,
whether you would risk it or not.

917
01:28:50,909 --> 01:28:52,524
THÉODEN:
When last I looked...

918
01:28:52,994 --> 01:28:56,612
...Théoden, not Aragorn,
was king of Rohan.

919
01:29:01,503 --> 01:29:03,084
[BURPS]

920
01:29:03,505 --> 01:29:05,746
Then what is the king's decision?

921
01:29:11,346 --> 01:29:12,756
HÁMA:
<i>By order of the king...</i>

922
01:29:12,848 --> 01:29:14,304
...the city must empty.

923
01:29:15,475 --> 01:29:18,342
We make for the refuge of Helm's Deep.

924
01:29:18,645 --> 01:29:22,604
Do not burden yourself with treasures.
Take only what provisions you need.

925
01:29:22,691 --> 01:29:24,272
GIMLI:
Helm's Deep.

926
01:29:24,359 --> 01:29:27,977
They flee to the mountains
when they should stand and fight.

927
01:29:28,071 --> 01:29:30,107
Who will defend them if not their king?

928
01:29:30,198 --> 01:29:32,735
He's only doing what he thinks
is best for his people.

929
01:29:32,826 --> 01:29:34,737
Helm's Deep has saved them
in the past.

930
01:29:34,828 --> 01:29:38,787
There is no way out of that ravine.
Théoden is walking into a trap.

931
01:29:38,874 --> 01:29:41,160
He thinks he's leading them to safety.

932
01:29:41,251 --> 01:29:43,458
What they will get is a massacre.

933
01:29:45,005 --> 01:29:47,496
Théoden has a strong will,
but I fear for him.

934
01:29:48,383 --> 01:29:51,750
I fear for the survival of Rohan.

935
01:29:52,178 --> 01:29:55,045
He will need you before the end,
Aragorn.

936
01:29:55,515 --> 01:29:58,302
The people of Rohan will need you.

937
01:29:58,685 --> 01:30:01,142
The defenses have to hold.

938
01:30:02,564 --> 01:30:04,304
They will hold.

939
01:30:08,320 --> 01:30:10,652
The Grey Pilgrim.

940
01:30:10,739 --> 01:30:13,446
That's what they used to call me.

941
01:30:13,533 --> 01:30:18,698
Three hundred lives of Men I've walked
this earth, and now I have no time.

942
01:30:20,290 --> 01:30:22,497
With luck, my search will not
be in vain.

943
01:30:23,043 --> 01:30:26,331
Look to my coming at first light
on the fifth day.

944
01:30:27,213 --> 01:30:29,955
At dawn, look to the east.

945
01:30:30,050 --> 01:30:31,631
Go.

946
01:30:45,565 --> 01:30:47,521
[HORSE NEIGHING]

947
01:30:58,954 --> 01:31:02,321
That horse is half mad, my lord.
There's nothing you can do. Leave him.

948
01:31:03,750 --> 01:31:05,832
[ARAGORN SPEAKING IN ELVISH]

949
01:31:41,371 --> 01:31:43,407
His name is Brego.

950
01:31:44,916 --> 01:31:46,907
He was my cousin's horse.

951
01:31:47,002 --> 01:31:48,867
Brego.

952
01:31:50,380 --> 01:31:53,122
[IN ELVISH]

953
01:31:53,591 --> 01:31:55,582
[CONTINUES SPEAKING IN ELVISH]

954
01:32:03,601 --> 01:32:06,058
I have heard of the magic of Elves...

955
01:32:06,146 --> 01:32:09,479
...but I did not look for it
in a Ranger from the North.

956
01:32:10,525 --> 01:32:12,937
You speak as one of their own.

957
01:32:14,738 --> 01:32:17,195
I was raised in Rivendell...

958
01:32:17,449 --> 01:32:18,985
...for a time.

959
01:32:22,287 --> 01:32:24,323
Turn this fellow free.

960
01:32:24,956 --> 01:32:27,447
He's seen enough of war.

961
01:32:39,220 --> 01:32:42,087
Gandalf the White.

962
01:32:42,182 --> 01:32:44,594
Gandalf the Fool!

963
01:32:45,935 --> 01:32:50,178
Does he seek to humble me
with his newfound piety?

964
01:32:51,149 --> 01:32:55,108
WORMTONGUE: There were three
who followed the wizard.

965
01:32:55,528 --> 01:33:00,864
An Elf, a Dwarf and a Man.

966
01:33:01,242 --> 01:33:04,029
You stink of horse.

967
01:33:09,292 --> 01:33:11,157
The Man...

968
01:33:13,213 --> 01:33:17,456
-...was he from Gondor?
-No, from the North.

969
01:33:17,550 --> 01:33:21,418
One of the Dúnedain Rangers,
I thought he was.

970
01:33:21,513 --> 01:33:23,344
His cloth was poor.

971
01:33:24,265 --> 01:33:29,385
And yet he bore a strange ring.

972
01:33:30,480 --> 01:33:34,064
Two serpents with emerald eyes.

973
01:33:34,150 --> 01:33:40,066
One devouring,
the other crowned with golden flowers.

974
01:33:40,156 --> 01:33:42,112
SARUMAN:
The Ring of Barahir.

975
01:33:43,076 --> 01:33:46,694
So Gandalf Greyhame
thinks he has found Isildur's heir.

976
01:33:46,788 --> 01:33:50,201
The lost king of Gondor.
He is a fool.

977
01:33:50,291 --> 01:33:53,078
The line was broken years ago.

978
01:33:54,504 --> 01:33:55,994
It matters not.

979
01:33:56,089 --> 01:33:58,705
The world of Men shall fall.

980
01:33:58,800 --> 01:34:00,711
It will begin at Edoras.

981
01:34:09,936 --> 01:34:11,892
I am ready, Gamling.

982
01:34:11,980 --> 01:34:14,517
Bring my horse.

983
01:34:17,652 --> 01:34:19,017
This is not a defeat.

984
01:34:21,447 --> 01:34:22,653
We will return.

985
01:34:28,121 --> 01:34:30,533
We will return.

986
01:34:53,897 --> 01:34:55,853
You have some skill with a blade.

987
01:35:04,365 --> 01:35:06,481
Women of this country learned long ago:

988
01:35:06,576 --> 01:35:09,283
Those without swords
can still die upon them.

989
01:35:09,370 --> 01:35:11,235
I fear neither death nor pain.

990
01:35:12,498 --> 01:35:14,614
What do you fear, my lady?

991
01:35:18,004 --> 01:35:19,835
A cage.

992
01:35:21,132 --> 01:35:25,000
To stay behind bars until use
and old age accept them.

993
01:35:25,094 --> 01:35:29,087
And all chance of valor has gone
beyond recall or desire.

994
01:35:32,477 --> 01:35:34,513
You're a daughter of kings...

995
01:35:35,772 --> 01:35:39,105
...a shieldmaiden of Rohan.

996
01:35:44,364 --> 01:35:46,901
I do not think that would be your fate.

997
01:36:19,941 --> 01:36:23,024
WORMTONGUE:
<i>Théoden will not stay at Edoras.</i>

998
01:36:23,111 --> 01:36:25,318
It's vulnerable. He knows this.

999
01:36:25,405 --> 01:36:28,317
He will expect an attack on the city.

1000
01:36:29,659 --> 01:36:32,947
They will flee to Helm's Deep...

1001
01:36:33,037 --> 01:36:35,403
...the great fortress of Rohan.

1002
01:36:36,666 --> 01:36:41,000
<i>It is a dangerous road to take</i>
<i>through the mountains.</i>

1003
01:36:42,463 --> 01:36:44,169
<i>They will be slow.</i>

1004
01:36:44,549 --> 01:36:48,963
They will have women and children
with them.

1005
01:36:52,849 --> 01:36:55,181
Send out your Warg-riders.

1006
01:36:55,685 --> 01:36:59,052
[GROWLING]

1007
01:37:09,991 --> 01:37:12,949
Hey, stinker, don't go getting
too far ahead.

1008
01:37:13,036 --> 01:37:15,778
-Why do you do that?
-What?

1009
01:37:15,872 --> 01:37:18,454
Call him names.
Run him down all the time.

1010
01:37:18,875 --> 01:37:20,911
Because.

1011
01:37:22,462 --> 01:37:24,623
Because that's what he is, Mr. Frodo.

1012
01:37:24,714 --> 01:37:26,955
There's naught left in him
but lies and deceit.

1013
01:37:27,383 --> 01:37:30,216
It's the Ring he wants.
It's all he cares about.

1014
01:37:30,303 --> 01:37:32,635
You have no idea what it did to him...

1015
01:37:32,722 --> 01:37:35,259
...what it's still doing to him.

1016
01:37:37,477 --> 01:37:39,593
I want to help him, Sam.

1017
01:37:39,687 --> 01:37:41,018
Why?

1018
01:37:46,319 --> 01:37:49,436
Because I have to believe
he can come back.

1019
01:37:53,743 --> 01:37:55,654
You can't save him, Mr. Frodo.

1020
01:37:55,745 --> 01:37:58,532
What do you know about it?
Nothing!

1021
01:38:05,463 --> 01:38:09,672
I'm sorry, Sam. I don't know
why I said that.

1022
01:38:10,510 --> 01:38:11,625
I do.

1023
01:38:13,679 --> 01:38:15,544
It's the Ring.

1024
01:38:16,099 --> 01:38:17,680
You can't take your eyes off it.

1025
01:38:18,393 --> 01:38:20,384
I've seen you.

1026
01:38:20,853 --> 01:38:24,687
You're not eating. You barely sleep.

1027
01:38:26,442 --> 01:38:28,728
It's taken hold of you, Mr. Frodo.

1028
01:38:28,820 --> 01:38:31,653
-You have to fight it.
-I know what I have to do, Sam.

1029
01:38:31,739 --> 01:38:34,697
The Ring was entrusted to me.
It's my task.

1030
01:38:34,784 --> 01:38:36,570
Mine! My own!

1031
01:38:37,412 --> 01:38:39,573
Can't you hear yourself?

1032
01:38:39,664 --> 01:38:41,370
Don't you know who you sound like?

1033
01:38:51,634 --> 01:38:53,795
GOLLUM:
We wants it.

1034
01:38:53,886 --> 01:38:56,673
We needs it.

1035
01:38:56,764 --> 01:39:01,679
Must have the precious.

1036
01:39:01,769 --> 01:39:05,261
They stole it from us.

1037
01:39:05,356 --> 01:39:08,814
Sneaky little Hobbitses.

1038
01:39:08,901 --> 01:39:12,860
Wicked. Tricksy. False.

1039
01:39:12,947 --> 01:39:16,314
SMÉAGOL:
No. Not master.

1040
01:39:16,409 --> 01:39:20,322
GOLLUM:
Yes, precious. False.

1041
01:39:20,413 --> 01:39:24,952
They will cheat you, hurt you, lie!

1042
01:39:26,085 --> 01:39:28,576
SMÉAGOL:
Master's my friend.

1043
01:39:28,671 --> 01:39:33,836
You don't have any friends.
Nobody likes you.

1044
01:39:35,052 --> 01:39:37,589
Not listening. I'm not listening.

1045
01:39:37,680 --> 01:39:41,719
You're a liar and a thief.

1046
01:39:42,351 --> 01:39:43,932
No.

1047
01:39:44,854 --> 01:39:47,721
Murderer.

1048
01:39:50,193 --> 01:39:51,273
Go away.

1049
01:39:51,360 --> 01:39:53,772
Go away?

1050
01:39:55,781 --> 01:39:58,614
I hate you.

1051
01:39:58,701 --> 01:40:01,158
I hate you.

1052
01:40:01,454 --> 01:40:04,787
Where would you be without me?
Gollum. Gollum.

1053
01:40:04,874 --> 01:40:06,785
I saved us.

1054
01:40:06,876 --> 01:40:11,461
It was me. We survived because of me.

1055
01:40:12,673 --> 01:40:16,257
Not anymore.

1056
01:40:17,595 --> 01:40:19,176
What did you say?

1057
01:40:21,224 --> 01:40:25,092
Master looks after us now.

1058
01:40:25,186 --> 01:40:28,724
We don't need you.

1059
01:40:29,440 --> 01:40:31,055
What?

1060
01:40:31,150 --> 01:40:32,981
Leave now...

1061
01:40:33,069 --> 01:40:36,937
...and never come back.

1062
01:40:37,031 --> 01:40:38,111
No.

1063
01:40:38,616 --> 01:40:42,825
Leave now and never come back.

1064
01:40:45,414 --> 01:40:51,330
Leave now and never come back!

1065
01:41:03,307 --> 01:41:06,049
We told him to go away.

1066
01:41:06,143 --> 01:41:09,180
And away he goes, precious.

1067
01:41:09,272 --> 01:41:11,354
Gone! Gone! Gone!

1068
01:41:11,440 --> 01:41:13,271
Sméagol is free!

1069
01:41:18,197 --> 01:41:19,733
SMÉAGOL:
Look.

1070
01:41:19,824 --> 01:41:24,363
Look. See what Sméagol finds?

1071
01:41:24,704 --> 01:41:27,867
[CHUCKLING]

1072
01:41:33,879 --> 01:41:35,335
They are young.

1073
01:41:35,423 --> 01:41:38,039
They are tender. They are nice.

1074
01:41:38,134 --> 01:41:41,718
Yes, they are. Eat them. Eat them!

1075
01:41:44,473 --> 01:41:46,009
You'll make him sick, you will...

1076
01:41:47,226 --> 01:41:49,467
...behaving like that.

1077
01:41:51,814 --> 01:41:54,601
There's only one way to eat
a brace of coneys.

1078
01:41:55,109 --> 01:41:57,225
[SMÉAGOL SHRIEKING]

1079
01:41:58,779 --> 01:42:00,360
What's it doing?

1080
01:42:01,073 --> 01:42:03,780
Stupid, fat Hobbit.

1081
01:42:03,868 --> 01:42:06,154
It ruins it.

1082
01:42:06,245 --> 01:42:09,908
What's to ruin? There's hardly any meat
on them.

1083
01:42:10,583 --> 01:42:13,541
[BIRD WHISTLING]

1084
01:42:14,045 --> 01:42:16,627
What we need is a few good taters.

1085
01:42:17,506 --> 01:42:20,589
What's taters, precious?

1086
01:42:20,676 --> 01:42:22,507
What's taters? Eh?

1087
01:42:22,595 --> 01:42:24,335
Po-ta-toes.

1088
01:42:24,680 --> 01:42:27,922
Boil them, mash them,
stick them in a stew.

1089
01:42:29,435 --> 01:42:34,930
Lovely, big, golden chips
with a nice piece of fried fish.

1090
01:42:36,233 --> 01:42:38,144
Even you couldn't say no to that.

1091
01:42:38,527 --> 01:42:40,688
Oh, yes, we could.

1092
01:42:40,780 --> 01:42:44,318
Spoil a nice fish.

1093
01:42:45,618 --> 01:42:48,280
Give it to us raw...

1094
01:42:48,371 --> 01:42:51,488
...and wriggling.

1095
01:42:51,582 --> 01:42:54,745
You keep nasty chips.

1096
01:42:55,670 --> 01:42:57,752
You're hopeless.

1097
01:43:10,267 --> 01:43:11,757
Mr. Frodo?

1098
01:43:29,662 --> 01:43:32,369
SAM: Who are they?
SMÉAGOL: Wicked Men.

1099
01:43:32,456 --> 01:43:34,947
Servants of Sauron.

1100
01:43:35,751 --> 01:43:37,992
They are called to Mordor.

1101
01:43:38,087 --> 01:43:41,204
The Dark One is gathering all armies
to him.

1102
01:43:41,298 --> 01:43:44,506
It won't be long now.
He will soon be ready.

1103
01:43:46,095 --> 01:43:49,758
-Ready to do what?
-To make his war.

1104
01:43:49,849 --> 01:43:55,094
The last war that will cover
all the world in Shadow.

1105
01:43:55,354 --> 01:43:57,219
We've got to get moving. Come on, Sam.

1106
01:43:57,314 --> 01:43:58,474
[OLIPHAUNT GROANS]

1107
01:43:58,566 --> 01:43:59,806
Mr. Frodo.

1108
01:44:00,317 --> 01:44:01,932
Look.

1109
01:44:05,614 --> 01:44:07,900
It's an oliphaunt.

1110
01:44:09,618 --> 01:44:12,485
[GROANING]

1111
01:44:16,125 --> 01:44:19,117
No one at home will believe this.

1112
01:44:23,382 --> 01:44:25,839
[BIRD WHISTLES]

1113
01:44:30,264 --> 01:44:32,129
Sméagol?

1114
01:44:34,894 --> 01:44:37,135
[ARROWS FLYING]

1115
01:44:37,229 --> 01:44:38,844
[SCREAMING]

1116
01:44:49,784 --> 01:44:51,900
[OLIPHAUNTS TRUMPETING]

1117
01:45:12,473 --> 01:45:14,964
We've lingered here too long.

1118
01:45:17,978 --> 01:45:19,309
Come on, Sam.

1119
01:45:31,367 --> 01:45:32,652
No!

1120
01:45:32,743 --> 01:45:35,450
Wait! We're innocent travelers!

1121
01:45:37,206 --> 01:45:42,326
There are no travelers in this land.
Only servants of the Dark Tower.

1122
01:45:42,419 --> 01:45:45,331
We are bound to an errand of secrecy.

1123
01:45:46,715 --> 01:45:50,128
Those that claim to oppose the enemy
would do well not to hinder us.

1124
01:45:50,219 --> 01:45:52,335
The enemy?

1125
01:45:54,390 --> 01:45:57,882
His sense of duty was no less
than yours, I deem.

1126
01:46:00,354 --> 01:46:02,470
You wonder what his name is...

1127
01:46:03,983 --> 01:46:06,224
...where he came from.

1128
01:46:08,237 --> 01:46:10,649
And if he was really evil at heart.

1129
01:46:12,324 --> 01:46:15,782
What lies or threats led him
on this long march from home.

1130
01:46:17,371 --> 01:46:19,862
If he would not rather have stayed there...

1131
01:46:22,042 --> 01:46:23,578
...in peace.

1132
01:46:27,131 --> 01:46:30,214
War will make corpses of us all.

1133
01:46:30,301 --> 01:46:32,383
Bind their hands.

1134
01:46:46,358 --> 01:46:49,191
GIMLI: It's true, you don't see
many Dwarf women.

1135
01:46:49,278 --> 01:46:52,987
And in fact, they are so alike
in voice and appearance...

1136
01:46:53,073 --> 01:46:56,315
...that they're often mistaken
for Dwarf men.

1137
01:46:56,660 --> 01:46:58,571
It's the beards.

1138
01:46:58,829 --> 01:47:00,945
This, in turn, has given rise
to the belief...

1139
01:47:01,040 --> 01:47:03,873
...that there are no Dwarf women...

1140
01:47:04,126 --> 01:47:08,369
...and that Dwarves just spring out
of holes in the ground...

1141
01:47:10,049 --> 01:47:11,459
...which is, of course, ridiculous.

1142
01:47:11,550 --> 01:47:13,040
[YELLS]

1143
01:47:18,015 --> 01:47:20,347
GIMLI:
It's all right. Nobody panic.

1144
01:47:20,726 --> 01:47:22,717
That was deliberate.
It was deliberate.

1145
01:47:24,647 --> 01:47:28,481
I haven't seen my niece smile
for a long time.

1146
01:47:28,776 --> 01:47:31,563
She was a girl when they brought
her father back dead.

1147
01:47:31,654 --> 01:47:34,020
Cut down by Orcs.

1148
01:47:34,114 --> 01:47:37,151
She watched her mother
succumb to grief.

1149
01:47:37,785 --> 01:47:42,529
Then she was left alone,
to tend her king in growing fear.

1150
01:47:42,623 --> 01:47:47,208
Doomed to wait upon an old man,
who should have loved her as a father.

1151
01:47:57,179 --> 01:47:59,591
Gimli.

1152
01:47:59,682 --> 01:48:01,843
No, I couldn't.

1153
01:48:01,934 --> 01:48:03,799
I really couldn't.

1154
01:48:08,315 --> 01:48:09,976
I made some stew.

1155
01:48:10,067 --> 01:48:13,400
It isn't much, but it's hot.

1156
01:48:21,203 --> 01:48:23,239
Thank you.

1157
01:48:43,767 --> 01:48:46,304
-It's good.
-Really?

1158
01:48:50,274 --> 01:48:53,641
My uncle told me a strange thing.

1159
01:48:54,945 --> 01:48:59,029
He said that you rode to war
with Thengel, my grandfather.

1160
01:48:59,450 --> 01:49:02,032
But he must be mistaken.

1161
01:49:02,119 --> 01:49:06,579
King Théoden has a good memory.
He was only a small child at the time.

1162
01:49:07,708 --> 01:49:10,950
Then you must be at least 60.

1163
01:49:13,005 --> 01:49:14,586
Seventy?

1164
01:49:15,007 --> 01:49:16,668
But you cannot be 80!

1165
01:49:20,012 --> 01:49:21,377
Eighty-seven.

1166
01:49:24,475 --> 01:49:26,591
You are one of the Dúnedain.

1167
01:49:27,644 --> 01:49:30,761
A descendant of Númenor,
blessed with long life.

1168
01:49:31,982 --> 01:49:34,598
It was said that your race
had passed into legend.

1169
01:49:35,277 --> 01:49:37,063
There are few of us left.

1170
01:49:37,154 --> 01:49:40,021
The Northern Kingdom
was destroyed long ago.

1171
01:49:40,783 --> 01:49:44,196
I'm sorry. Please, eat.

1172
01:49:58,842 --> 01:50:03,006
ARWEN: <i>The light of the Evenstar</i>
<i>does not wax and wane.</i>

1173
01:50:03,764 --> 01:50:07,222
<i>It is mine to give to whom I will.</i>

1174
01:50:09,019 --> 01:50:11,431
<i>Like my heart.</i>

1175
01:50:12,856 --> 01:50:15,598
<i>Go to sleep.</i>

1176
01:50:15,692 --> 01:50:18,229
I am asleep.

1177
01:50:24,701 --> 01:50:26,657
This is a dream.

1178
01:50:28,872 --> 01:50:32,080
Then it is a good dream.

1179
01:50:44,096 --> 01:50:46,178
Sleep.

1180
01:51:11,248 --> 01:51:12,784
[IN ELVISH]

1181
01:51:18,422 --> 01:51:20,413
[IN ELVISH]

1182
01:51:49,161 --> 01:51:51,072
[IN ENGLISH]
Arwen....

1183
01:52:40,545 --> 01:52:42,376
ÉOWYN:
Where is she?

1184
01:52:43,548 --> 01:52:45,960
The woman who gave you that jewel.

1185
01:52:49,304 --> 01:52:52,046
ELROND:
<i>Our time here is ending.</i>

1186
01:52:52,724 --> 01:52:55,306
Arwen's time is ending.

1187
01:52:56,019 --> 01:52:57,350
Let her go.

1188
01:52:57,437 --> 01:52:59,519
Let her take the ship into the west.

1189
01:52:59,606 --> 01:53:02,769
Let her bear away her love for you
to the Undying Lands.

1190
01:53:02,859 --> 01:53:04,690
There it will be ever green.

1191
01:53:06,196 --> 01:53:08,562
But never more than memory.

1192
01:53:09,825 --> 01:53:12,942
I will not leave my daughter here
to die.

1193
01:53:13,036 --> 01:53:16,745
-She stays because she still has hope.
-She stays for you.

1194
01:53:16,832 --> 01:53:19,198
She belongs with her people.

1195
01:53:31,638 --> 01:53:33,629
[IN ELVISH]

1196
01:53:40,731 --> 01:53:43,017
[IN ELVISH]

1197
01:54:07,507 --> 01:54:09,338
[IN ENGLISH]
Why are you saying this?

1198
01:54:10,927 --> 01:54:14,090
[IN ENGLISH]
I am mortal. You are Elf-kind.

1199
01:54:15,557 --> 01:54:18,219
It was a dream, Arwen.

1200
01:54:18,643 --> 01:54:20,008
Nothing more.

1201
01:54:21,396 --> 01:54:24,604
I don't believe you.

1202
01:54:33,617 --> 01:54:35,448
This belongs to you.

1203
01:54:38,205 --> 01:54:39,786
It was a gift.

1204
01:54:42,459 --> 01:54:43,949
Keep it.

1205
01:54:46,463 --> 01:54:47,669
ÉOWYN:
My lord?

1206
01:54:50,467 --> 01:54:55,052
She is sailing to the Undying Lands
with all that is left of her kin.

1207
01:55:16,743 --> 01:55:18,028
[HORSE NEIGHS]

1208
01:55:18,495 --> 01:55:19,985
What is it?

1209
01:55:21,498 --> 01:55:23,534
-Háma?
-I'm not sure.

1210
01:55:29,172 --> 01:55:32,005
[YELLING AND ROARING]

1211
01:55:40,100 --> 01:55:42,182
Wargs!

1212
01:55:54,698 --> 01:55:56,359
A scout!

1213
01:56:02,706 --> 01:56:05,197
-What is it? What do you see?
-Warg! We're under attack!

1214
01:56:06,543 --> 01:56:08,750
Get them out of here!

1215
01:56:13,508 --> 01:56:15,544
All riders to the head of the column.

1216
01:56:16,219 --> 01:56:18,255
GIMLI:
Come on. Get me up here. I'm a rider.

1217
01:56:18,346 --> 01:56:20,132
Come on!

1218
01:56:22,100 --> 01:56:25,308
[WARGS BARKING]

1219
01:56:31,943 --> 01:56:34,434
You must lead the people
to Helm's Deep, and make haste.

1220
01:56:34,529 --> 01:56:36,065
-I can fight.
-No!

1221
01:56:38,742 --> 01:56:40,824
You must do this, for me.

1222
01:56:42,829 --> 01:56:44,410
Follow me! Hyah!

1223
01:56:47,918 --> 01:56:52,287
GIMLI: Forward. I mean, charge forward.
ÉOWYN: Make for the lower ground!

1224
01:56:52,380 --> 01:56:55,087
-That's it! Go on!
-Stay together!

1225
01:58:07,330 --> 01:58:09,616
GIMLI:
Bring your pretty face to my ax.

1226
01:58:12,419 --> 01:58:14,000
That one counts as mine!

1227
01:58:30,687 --> 01:58:32,302
Stinking creature.

1228
01:58:37,402 --> 01:58:39,017
[SNIFFS]

1229
01:58:42,324 --> 01:58:44,360
[GRUNTING]

1230
01:59:44,260 --> 01:59:45,670
[YELLS]

1231
01:59:59,567 --> 02:00:01,432
Aragorn!

1232
02:00:06,157 --> 02:00:07,613
Aragorn?

1233
02:00:13,456 --> 02:00:16,198
[LAUGHING]

1234
02:00:21,631 --> 02:00:24,589
Tell me what happened
and I will ease your passing.

1235
02:00:24,676 --> 02:00:26,132
He's...

1236
02:00:26,720 --> 02:00:28,301
...dead.

1237
02:00:28,972 --> 02:00:31,839
He took a little tumble off the cliff.

1238
02:00:35,478 --> 02:00:36,763
You lie.

1239
02:00:37,272 --> 02:00:39,684
[CHOKES]

1240
02:01:10,680 --> 02:01:12,295
Get the wounded on horses.

1241
02:01:13,600 --> 02:01:16,763
The wolves of Isengard will return.

1242
02:01:17,187 --> 02:01:19,303
Leave the dead.

1243
02:01:26,696 --> 02:01:28,186
Come.

1244
02:01:38,374 --> 02:01:40,035
WOMAN 1: At last!
WOMAN 2: Helm's Deep.

1245
02:01:40,126 --> 02:01:43,038
WOMAN 3:
There it is, Helm's Deep.

1246
02:01:45,590 --> 02:01:47,421
WOMAN 4:
We're safe!

1247
02:01:48,927 --> 02:01:51,839
We're safe, my lady.

1248
02:01:51,930 --> 02:01:53,170
Thank you.

1249
02:02:37,517 --> 02:02:38,973
FREDA: Mama!
MORWEN: Éothain!

1250
02:02:39,060 --> 02:02:40,641
Freda!

1251
02:02:46,401 --> 02:02:49,234
-Where is the rest?
-This is all we could save, my lady.

1252
02:02:53,074 --> 02:02:54,439
Take it to the caves.

1253
02:02:54,534 --> 02:02:57,401
MAN:
Make way for the king.

1254
02:02:59,289 --> 02:03:02,247
GAMLING: Make way for Théoden.
Make way for the king.

1255
02:03:10,133 --> 02:03:13,876
So few. So few of you have returned.

1256
02:03:16,639 --> 02:03:18,925
Our people are safe.

1257
02:03:20,268 --> 02:03:22,805
We have paid for it with many lives.

1258
02:03:23,646 --> 02:03:25,182
GIMLI:
My lady.

1259
02:03:28,902 --> 02:03:31,188
Lord Aragorn...

1260
02:03:31,279 --> 02:03:32,564
...where is he?

1261
02:03:34,574 --> 02:03:36,110
He fell.

1262
02:03:58,806 --> 02:04:01,798
Draw all our forces behind the wall.

1263
02:04:01,893 --> 02:04:04,851
Bar the gate.
And set a watch on the surround.

1264
02:04:05,104 --> 02:04:08,221
GAMLING: What of those who cannot
fight, my lord? The women and children?

1265
02:04:08,316 --> 02:04:10,978
THÉODEN:
Get them into the caves.

1266
02:04:11,861 --> 02:04:16,696
Saruman's arm will have grown long
indeed if he thinks he can reach us here.

1267
02:04:18,743 --> 02:04:22,201
WORMTONGUE:
<i>Helm's Deep has one weakness.</i>

1268
02:04:22,288 --> 02:04:24,700
<i>Its outer wall is solid rock...</i>

1269
02:04:24,791 --> 02:04:27,954
<i>...but for a small culvert</i>
<i>at its base...</i>

1270
02:04:28,044 --> 02:04:30,877
<i>...which is little more than a drain.</i>

1271
02:04:33,716 --> 02:04:37,925
How? How can fire undo stone?

1272
02:04:38,012 --> 02:04:42,597
What kind of device
could bring down the wall?

1273
02:04:46,229 --> 02:04:50,268
SARUMAN: If the wall is breached,
Helm's Deep will fall.

1274
02:04:50,358 --> 02:04:53,942
Even if it is breached, it would take
a number beyond reckoning...

1275
02:04:54,028 --> 02:04:56,690
...thousands, to storm the Keep.

1276
02:04:56,781 --> 02:04:58,271
SARUMAN:
Tens of thousands.

1277
02:04:58,366 --> 02:05:02,530
WORMTONGUE:
But, my lord, there is no such force.

1278
02:05:02,620 --> 02:05:04,451
[HORNS SOUNDING]

1279
02:05:04,747 --> 02:05:08,114
[ARMY CHEERING]

1280
02:05:14,424 --> 02:05:17,541
A new power is rising.

1281
02:05:17,635 --> 02:05:20,672
Its victory is at hand.

1282
02:05:26,352 --> 02:05:28,434
This night...

1283
02:05:28,855 --> 02:05:33,224
...the land will be stained
with the blood of Rohan!

1284
02:05:33,317 --> 02:05:36,730
March to Helm's Deep!

1285
02:05:36,821 --> 02:05:40,359
Leave none alive!

1286
02:05:42,869 --> 02:05:45,360
To war!

1287
02:05:49,292 --> 02:05:53,752
There will be no dawn for Men.

1288
02:06:10,938 --> 02:06:13,020
Look. There's smoke to the south.

1289
02:06:13,107 --> 02:06:16,395
There is always smoke rising...

1290
02:06:16,486 --> 02:06:20,354
...from Isengard these days.

1291
02:06:20,615 --> 02:06:22,276
Isengard?

1292
02:06:22,366 --> 02:06:24,277
TREEBEARD:
There was a time...

1293
02:06:24,619 --> 02:06:28,203
...when Saruman would walk in my woods.

1294
02:06:28,289 --> 02:06:31,656
But now he has a mind of metal...

1295
02:06:32,335 --> 02:06:34,792
...and wheels.

1296
02:06:35,546 --> 02:06:40,085
He no longer cares for growing things.

1297
02:06:40,176 --> 02:06:42,007
What is it?

1298
02:06:47,016 --> 02:06:49,257
It's Saruman's army.

1299
02:06:49,352 --> 02:06:50,967
The war has started.

1300
02:07:29,267 --> 02:07:33,636
ARWEN: <i>May the grace of the Valar</i>
<i>protect you.</i>

1301
02:08:05,928 --> 02:08:07,793
Brego.

1302
02:08:33,915 --> 02:08:35,075
ELROND:
Arwen.

1303
02:08:36,417 --> 02:08:38,282
[IN ELVISH]

1304
02:08:44,967 --> 02:08:46,753
I have made my choice.

1305
02:08:53,184 --> 02:08:56,051
[IN ENGLISH]
He is not coming back.

1306
02:08:57,480 --> 02:09:00,813
Why do you linger here
when there is no hope?

1307
02:09:01,734 --> 02:09:04,726
There is still hope.

1308
02:09:08,866 --> 02:09:12,654
If Aragorn survives this war,
you will still be parted.

1309
02:09:16,040 --> 02:09:19,032
If Sauron is defeated
and Aragorn made king...

1310
02:09:19,126 --> 02:09:21,708
...and all that you hope for
comes true...

1311
02:09:21,796 --> 02:09:26,540
...you will still have to taste
the bitterness of mortality.

1312
02:09:26,842 --> 02:09:29,879
Whether by the sword
or the slow decay of time...

1313
02:09:29,971 --> 02:09:32,929
...Aragorn will die.

1314
02:09:35,768 --> 02:09:38,384
<i>And there will be no comfort</i>
<i>for you...</i>

1315
02:09:38,479 --> 02:09:42,722
<i>...no comfort to ease the pain</i>
<i>of his passing.</i>

1316
02:09:45,528 --> 02:09:48,315
<i>He will come to death...</i>

1317
02:09:48,406 --> 02:09:51,068
<i>...an image of the splendor</i>
<i>of the kings of Men...</i>

1318
02:09:51,158 --> 02:09:55,868
<i>...in glory undimmed before</i>
<i>the breaking of the world.</i>

1319
02:10:04,964 --> 02:10:08,923
<i>But you, my daughter...</i>

1320
02:10:09,719 --> 02:10:14,804
<i>...you will linger on in darkness</i>
<i>and in doubt...</i>

1321
02:10:14,890 --> 02:10:19,008
<i>...as nightfall in winter</i>
<i>that comes without a star.</i>

1322
02:10:21,397 --> 02:10:23,854
<i>Here you will dwell...</i>

1323
02:10:23,941 --> 02:10:28,901
<i>...bound to your grief</i>
<i>under the fading trees...</i>

1324
02:10:30,614 --> 02:10:32,650
<i>...until all the world is changed...</i>

1325
02:10:32,742 --> 02:10:37,281
...and the long years of your life
are utterly spent.

1326
02:10:45,838 --> 02:10:46,998
Arwen.

1327
02:10:53,637 --> 02:10:55,923
There is nothing for you here...

1328
02:10:56,599 --> 02:10:58,681
...only death.

1329
02:11:19,455 --> 02:11:21,446
[IN ELVISH]

1330
02:11:24,210 --> 02:11:25,950
[IN ELVISH]

1331
02:12:17,221 --> 02:12:20,384
[GALADRIEL SPEAKING IN ELVISH]

1332
02:12:32,111 --> 02:12:35,774
GALADRIEL [IN ENGLISH]:
<i>The power of the enemy is growing.</i>

1333
02:12:35,865 --> 02:12:38,572
<i>Sauron will use his puppet,</i>
<i>Saruman...</i>

1334
02:12:38,659 --> 02:12:42,151
<i>...to destroy the people of Rohan.</i>

1335
02:12:44,206 --> 02:12:47,869
<i>Isengard has been unleashed.</i>

1336
02:12:52,173 --> 02:12:55,540
<i>The Eye of Sauron now turns</i>
<i>to Gondor...</i>

1337
02:12:56,677 --> 02:12:59,714
<i>...the last free kingdom of Men.</i>

1338
02:12:59,805 --> 02:13:04,219
<i>His war on this country</i>
<i>will come swiftly.</i>

1339
02:13:07,938 --> 02:13:11,101
<i>He senses the Ring is close.</i>

1340
02:13:11,192 --> 02:13:14,730
<i>The strength of the Ring-bearer</i>
<i>is failing.</i>

1341
02:13:14,820 --> 02:13:18,904
<i>In his heart, Frodo begins</i>
<i>to understand...</i>

1342
02:13:20,451 --> 02:13:24,364
...the quest will claim his life.

1343
02:13:24,455 --> 02:13:26,662
You know this.

1344
02:13:27,249 --> 02:13:30,082
<i>You have foreseen it.</i>

1345
02:13:32,213 --> 02:13:35,671
<i>It is the risk we all took.</i>

1346
02:13:40,054 --> 02:13:44,263
<i>In the gathering dark, the will</i>
<i>of the Ring grows strong.</i>

1347
02:13:45,434 --> 02:13:49,894
<i>It works hard now to find its way back</i>
<i>into the hands of Men.</i>

1348
02:13:49,980 --> 02:13:55,566
<i>Men, who are so easily seduced</i>
<i>by its power.</i>

1349
02:13:55,653 --> 02:13:59,316
<i>The young captain of Gondor</i>
<i>has but to extend his hand...</i>

1350
02:13:59,406 --> 02:14:03,524
<i>...take the Ring for his own,</i>
<i>and the world will fall.</i>

1351
02:14:05,955 --> 02:14:07,820
<i>It is close now.</i>

1352
02:14:07,915 --> 02:14:12,204
<i>So close to achieving its goal.</i>

1353
02:14:13,087 --> 02:14:14,998
[ROARING]

1354
02:14:15,297 --> 02:14:19,006
<i>For Sauron will have dominion</i>
<i>over all life on this Earth...</i>

1355
02:14:19,093 --> 02:14:23,257
<i>...even unto the ending</i>
<i>of the world.</i>

1356
02:14:25,099 --> 02:14:27,010
<i>The time of the Elves...</i>

1357
02:14:27,101 --> 02:14:29,057
<i>...is over.</i>

1358
02:14:29,895 --> 02:14:33,479
<i>Do we leave Middle-earth</i>
<i>to its fate?</i>

1359
02:14:35,442 --> 02:14:38,684
<i>Do we let them stand alone?</i>

1360
02:14:43,325 --> 02:14:44,690
What news?

1361
02:14:44,785 --> 02:14:47,697
Our scouts report Saruman
has attacked Rohan.

1362
02:14:47,788 --> 02:14:50,700
Théoden's people have fled
to Helm's Deep.

1363
02:14:50,791 --> 02:14:54,909
But we must look to our own borders.
Faramir, Orcs are on the move.

1364
02:14:55,004 --> 02:14:57,461
Sauron is marshaling an army.

1365
02:14:57,798 --> 02:14:59,959
Easterlings and Southrons
are at the Black Gate.

1366
02:15:00,050 --> 02:15:03,508
-How many?
-Some thousands. More come every day.

1367
02:15:04,597 --> 02:15:08,215
-Who's covering the river to the north?
-We pulled 500 men at Osgiliath.

1368
02:15:08,309 --> 02:15:11,392
If their city is attacked,
we won't hold it.

1369
02:15:13,522 --> 02:15:15,729
FARAMIR:
Saruman attacks from Isengard.

1370
02:15:15,816 --> 02:15:18,558
Sauron from Mordor.

1371
02:15:19,862 --> 02:15:23,150
The fight will come to Men
on both fronts.

1372
02:15:23,240 --> 02:15:25,026
Gondor is weak.

1373
02:15:25,117 --> 02:15:28,280
Sauron will strike us soon.

1374
02:15:29,038 --> 02:15:30,869
And he will strike hard.

1375
02:15:31,332 --> 02:15:35,416
He knows now we do not have
the strength to repel him.

1376
02:15:49,350 --> 02:15:51,591
My men tell me that you are Orc spies.

1377
02:15:51,685 --> 02:15:54,518
Spies? Now wait just a minute.

1378
02:15:54,605 --> 02:15:56,891
Well, if you're not spies,
then who are you?

1379
02:16:03,781 --> 02:16:05,521
Speak.

1380
02:16:06,617 --> 02:16:09,233
We are Hobbits of the Shire.

1381
02:16:09,578 --> 02:16:12,570
Frodo Baggins is my name,
and this is Samwise Gamgee.

1382
02:16:12,998 --> 02:16:14,579
Your bodyguard?

1383
02:16:14,667 --> 02:16:16,498
His gardener.

1384
02:16:17,086 --> 02:16:19,077
And where is your skulking friend?

1385
02:16:20,589 --> 02:16:22,921
That gangrel creature.

1386
02:16:23,258 --> 02:16:25,214
He had an ill-favored look.

1387
02:16:26,929 --> 02:16:28,840
There was no other.

1388
02:16:32,935 --> 02:16:35,267
We set out from Rivendell
with seven companions.

1389
02:16:38,607 --> 02:16:41,690
One we lost in Moria...

1390
02:16:42,778 --> 02:16:44,314
...two were my kin...

1391
02:16:44,405 --> 02:16:48,239
...a Dwarf there was also.
And an Elf and two Men.

1392
02:16:48,325 --> 02:16:52,284
Aragorn, son of Arathorn,
and Boromir of Gondor.

1393
02:16:57,292 --> 02:16:59,032
You're a friend of Boromir?

1394
02:17:01,463 --> 02:17:02,953
Yes.

1395
02:17:04,049 --> 02:17:05,129
For my part.

1396
02:17:11,640 --> 02:17:14,598
It will grieve you then to learn
that he is dead.

1397
02:17:16,645 --> 02:17:18,135
Dead?

1398
02:17:18,230 --> 02:17:20,312
How? When?

1399
02:17:20,566 --> 02:17:23,228
As one of his companions,
I'd hoped you would tell me.

1400
02:17:23,527 --> 02:17:27,361
If something has happened to Boromir,
we would have you tell us.

1401
02:17:30,117 --> 02:17:36,659
His horn washed up upon the riverbank,
about six days past.

1402
02:17:36,749 --> 02:17:39,866
It was cloven in two.

1403
02:17:41,545 --> 02:17:44,958
But more than this, I know it in my heart.

1404
02:17:47,009 --> 02:17:48,795
He was my brother.

1405
02:18:35,516 --> 02:18:37,552
[MEN CHEERING]

1406
02:18:37,643 --> 02:18:40,726
MEN:
Boromir!

1407
02:18:41,230 --> 02:18:43,095
Boromir!

1408
02:18:47,361 --> 02:18:51,149
This city was once the jewel
of our kingdom.

1409
02:18:51,240 --> 02:18:54,983
A place of light and beauty and music.

1410
02:18:55,077 --> 02:18:57,443
And so it shall be once more!

1411
02:18:59,998 --> 02:19:02,705
Let the armies of Mordor know this:

1412
02:19:02,793 --> 02:19:07,207
Never again will the land of my people
fall into enemy hands.

1413
02:19:11,009 --> 02:19:16,675
This city of Osgiliath
has been reclaimed for Gondor!

1414
02:19:17,057 --> 02:19:19,048
-For Gondor!
-For Gondor!

1415
02:19:19,142 --> 02:19:22,009
-For Gondor!
-For Gondor!

1416
02:19:30,737 --> 02:19:33,524
Good speech. Nice and short.

1417
02:19:33,615 --> 02:19:36,573
Leaves more time for drinking!

1418
02:19:36,869 --> 02:19:41,112
Break out the ale! These men are thirsty!

1419
02:19:44,585 --> 02:19:46,792
Remember today, little brother.

1420
02:19:46,879 --> 02:19:49,916
Today, life is good.

1421
02:19:54,094 --> 02:19:55,675
What?

1422
02:19:56,054 --> 02:19:57,510
He's here.

1423
02:20:00,726 --> 02:20:03,809
-Moment of peace, can he not give us that?
DENETHOR: Where is he?

1424
02:20:03,896 --> 02:20:07,388
Where is Gondor's finest?
Where's my first-born?

1425
02:20:07,941 --> 02:20:09,647
Father!

1426
02:20:14,489 --> 02:20:16,901
They say you vanquished the enemy
almost single-handedly.

1427
02:20:16,992 --> 02:20:20,450
They exaggerate.
The victory belongs to Faramir also.

1428
02:20:21,914 --> 02:20:24,826
But for Faramir, this city
would still be standing.

1429
02:20:25,626 --> 02:20:27,958
Were you not entrusted to protect it?

1430
02:20:28,045 --> 02:20:30,161
I would have done,
but our numbers were too few.

1431
02:20:30,255 --> 02:20:31,995
Oh, too few.

1432
02:20:32,507 --> 02:20:34,873
You let the enemy walk in
and take it on a whim.

1433
02:20:37,095 --> 02:20:40,212
Always you cast a poor reflection on me.

1434
02:20:40,307 --> 02:20:42,639
That is not my intent.

1435
02:20:42,726 --> 02:20:46,514
You give him no credit,
and yet he tries to do your will.

1436
02:20:49,900 --> 02:20:52,858
-He loves you, Father.
-Do not trouble me with Faramir...

1437
02:20:52,945 --> 02:20:55,778
...I know his uses, and they are few.

1438
02:20:55,864 --> 02:20:59,527
We have more urgent things to speak of.

1439
02:21:00,702 --> 02:21:03,159
Elrond of Rivendell has called a meeting.

1440
02:21:03,246 --> 02:21:06,204
He will not say why,
but I have guessed its purpose.

1441
02:21:06,291 --> 02:21:10,125
It is rumored that the weapon
of the enemy has been found.

1442
02:21:12,339 --> 02:21:14,625
The One Ring.

1443
02:21:17,386 --> 02:21:22,096
-Isildur's Bane.
-It has fallen into the hands of the Elves.

1444
02:21:22,182 --> 02:21:25,891
Everyone will try to claim it:
Men, Dwarves, wizards.

1445
02:21:25,978 --> 02:21:30,142
We cannot let that happen.
This thing must come to Gondor.

1446
02:21:31,942 --> 02:21:34,649
-Gondor.
-It's dangerous, I know.

1447
02:21:34,736 --> 02:21:38,524
Ever the Ring will seek to corrupt
the hearts of lesser Men.

1448
02:21:38,615 --> 02:21:42,654
But you, you are strong.
And our need is great.

1449
02:21:42,744 --> 02:21:48,114
It is our blood which is being spilled,
our people who are dying.

1450
02:21:48,208 --> 02:21:53,373
Sauron is biding his time.
He's massing fresh armies.

1451
02:21:53,463 --> 02:21:55,044
He will return.

1452
02:21:55,132 --> 02:21:58,966
And when he does,
we will be powerless to stop him.

1453
02:21:59,052 --> 02:22:01,634
You must go.

1454
02:22:02,806 --> 02:22:04,922
Bring me back this mighty gift.

1455
02:22:05,767 --> 02:22:11,182
No. My place is here with my people.
Not in Rivendell.

1456
02:22:11,440 --> 02:22:15,149
-Would you deny your own father?
-If there is need to go to Rivendell...

1457
02:22:15,235 --> 02:22:18,272
-...send me in his stead.
-You?

1458
02:22:19,448 --> 02:22:21,404
Oh, I see.

1459
02:22:21,491 --> 02:22:25,734
A chance for Faramir, captain of Gondor,
to show his quality.

1460
02:22:26,163 --> 02:22:28,199
I think not.

1461
02:22:28,290 --> 02:22:31,248
I trust this mission only to your brother.

1462
02:22:31,334 --> 02:22:34,292
The one who will not fail me.

1463
02:22:51,438 --> 02:22:54,601
Remember today, little brother.

1464
02:23:12,959 --> 02:23:14,950
MAN:
Captain Faramir!

1465
02:23:16,213 --> 02:23:18,329
[WHISPERING]
We found the third one.

1466
02:23:23,929 --> 02:23:25,760
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

1467
02:23:29,851 --> 02:23:31,842
You must come with me. Now.

1468
02:23:43,073 --> 02:23:44,188
Down there.

1469
02:23:59,089 --> 02:24:01,956
To enter the Forbidden Pool
bears the penalty of death.

1470
02:24:12,561 --> 02:24:14,051
They wait for my command.

1471
02:24:19,568 --> 02:24:20,648
Shall I shoot?

1472
02:24:21,903 --> 02:24:24,940
<i>The rock and pool</i>
<i>Is nice and cool</i>

1473
02:24:25,031 --> 02:24:26,896
<i>So juicy sweet</i>

1474
02:24:27,576 --> 02:24:30,568
<i>Our only wish</i>
<i>To catch a fish</i>

1475
02:24:30,662 --> 02:24:33,404
<i>So juicy sweet</i>

1476
02:24:36,877 --> 02:24:38,583
[YELLS]

1477
02:24:40,422 --> 02:24:41,787
Wait.

1478
02:24:43,300 --> 02:24:46,133
This creature is bound to me.

1479
02:24:46,761 --> 02:24:48,672
And I to him.

1480
02:24:51,933 --> 02:24:53,264
He is our guide.

1481
02:24:57,981 --> 02:24:59,437
Please...

1482
02:24:59,524 --> 02:25:01,435
...let me go down to him.

1483
02:25:12,704 --> 02:25:14,365
Sméagol.

1484
02:25:15,373 --> 02:25:17,614
Master is here.

1485
02:25:18,793 --> 02:25:19,953
Come, Sméagol.

1486
02:25:22,797 --> 02:25:25,459
Trust master. Come.

1487
02:25:28,637 --> 02:25:32,471
We must go now?

1488
02:25:32,807 --> 02:25:36,299
Sméagol, you must trust master.

1489
02:25:36,394 --> 02:25:37,804
Follow me. Come on.

1490
02:25:39,022 --> 02:25:40,637
Come.

1491
02:25:43,151 --> 02:25:44,311
Come, Sméagol.

1492
02:25:44,819 --> 02:25:46,901
Nice Sméagol. That's it.

1493
02:25:47,405 --> 02:25:48,941
Come on.

1494
02:25:50,784 --> 02:25:52,024
[FOOTSTEP]

1495
02:25:53,328 --> 02:25:55,034
Don't hurt him!

1496
02:25:55,121 --> 02:25:57,954
Sméagol, don't struggle.
Sméagol, listen to me.

1497
02:25:58,041 --> 02:25:59,372
Master!

1498
02:26:02,462 --> 02:26:04,828
[MUFFLED CRIES]

1499
02:26:10,470 --> 02:26:14,179
[GRUNTING AND PANTING]

1500
02:26:24,567 --> 02:26:26,899
That's enough.

1501
02:26:30,573 --> 02:26:32,780
Where are you leading them?

1502
02:26:32,867 --> 02:26:34,403
[CRYING]

1503
02:26:34,494 --> 02:26:36,200
FARAMIR:
Answer me.

1504
02:26:37,038 --> 02:26:40,246
GOLLUM:
Sméagol.

1505
02:26:40,583 --> 02:26:42,790
[CRYING]

1506
02:26:43,712 --> 02:26:48,456
GOLLUM:
Why does it cry, Sméagol?

1507
02:26:49,718 --> 02:26:52,380
SMÉAGOL:
Cruel Men hurts us.

1508
02:26:52,470 --> 02:26:55,553
Master tricksed us.

1509
02:26:55,640 --> 02:26:59,224
GOLLUM:
Of course he did.

1510
02:26:59,602 --> 02:27:03,345
I told you he was tricksy.

1511
02:27:03,440 --> 02:27:06,557
I told you he was false.

1512
02:27:06,651 --> 02:27:09,438
SMÉAGOL:
Master is our friend.

1513
02:27:09,529 --> 02:27:11,941
Our friend.

1514
02:27:12,032 --> 02:27:14,273
GOLLUM:
Master betrayed us.

1515
02:27:14,367 --> 02:27:17,404
SMÉAGOL:
No. Not its business.

1516
02:27:18,496 --> 02:27:20,953
Leave us alone!

1517
02:27:21,041 --> 02:27:23,532
GOLLUM:
Filthy little Hobbitses!

1518
02:27:23,626 --> 02:27:25,992
They stole it from us!

1519
02:27:26,087 --> 02:27:27,577
SMÉAGOL:
No. No.

1520
02:27:28,131 --> 02:27:29,746
What did they steal?

1521
02:27:31,926 --> 02:27:37,262
GOLLUM:
My precious!

1522
02:27:37,724 --> 02:27:40,261
[YELLS]

1523
02:27:40,935 --> 02:27:42,596
We have to get out of here.

1524
02:27:43,188 --> 02:27:45,144
You go. Go, now.

1525
02:27:47,776 --> 02:27:49,607
You can do it.

1526
02:27:51,071 --> 02:27:52,561
Use the Ring, Mr. Frodo.

1527
02:27:52,655 --> 02:27:54,520
Just this once.

1528
02:27:54,616 --> 02:27:56,447
Put it on.

1529
02:27:56,868 --> 02:27:58,904
Disappear.

1530
02:27:59,954 --> 02:28:01,034
I can't.

1531
02:28:04,125 --> 02:28:06,332
You were right, Sam.

1532
02:28:07,796 --> 02:28:10,287
You tried to tell me but....

1533
02:28:14,969 --> 02:28:17,130
I'm sorry.

1534
02:28:21,684 --> 02:28:24,551
The Ring's taking me, Sam.

1535
02:28:25,980 --> 02:28:27,686
If I put it on...

1536
02:28:27,774 --> 02:28:30,140
...he'll find me.

1537
02:28:31,820 --> 02:28:33,776
He'll see.

1538
02:28:34,989 --> 02:28:36,980
Mr. Frodo....

1539
02:28:41,913 --> 02:28:46,156
So this is the answer
to all the riddles.

1540
02:28:48,378 --> 02:28:51,415
Here in the Wild I have you...

1541
02:28:51,506 --> 02:28:53,497
...two Halflings...

1542
02:28:53,591 --> 02:28:56,799
...and a host of men at my call.

1543
02:29:00,098 --> 02:29:03,590
The Ring of Power within my grasp.

1544
02:29:13,278 --> 02:29:17,021
A chance for Faramir,
captain of Gondor...

1545
02:29:18,616 --> 02:29:21,653
...to show his quality.

1546
02:29:39,179 --> 02:29:41,841
[VOICE OF THE RING WHISPERING]

1547
02:29:42,765 --> 02:29:44,380
No!

1548
02:29:47,562 --> 02:29:48,927
Stop it!

1549
02:29:49,022 --> 02:29:50,102
Leave him alone.

1550
02:29:51,441 --> 02:29:53,932
Don't you understand?

1551
02:29:55,236 --> 02:29:57,192
He's got to destroy it!

1552
02:29:57,280 --> 02:30:00,613
That's where we're going, into Mordor.

1553
02:30:00,700 --> 02:30:02,406
To the Mountain of Fire!

1554
02:30:03,453 --> 02:30:06,616
Osgiliath is under attack.
They call for reinforcements.

1555
02:30:06,706 --> 02:30:09,743
SAM:
Please. It's such a burden.

1556
02:30:11,920 --> 02:30:14,002
Will you not help him?

1557
02:30:15,340 --> 02:30:17,251
Captain?

1558
02:30:17,926 --> 02:30:20,133
Prepare to leave.

1559
02:30:25,099 --> 02:30:27,511
The Ring will go to Gondor.

1560
02:30:37,904 --> 02:30:41,146
[DISTANT MARCHING FOOTSTEPS]

1561
02:31:27,829 --> 02:31:30,912
[SPEAKS IN ELVISH]

1562
02:31:40,508 --> 02:31:43,215
WOMAN: He's alive!
GIMLI: Where is he? Where is he?

1563
02:31:43,303 --> 02:31:46,420
Get out of the way!
I'm going to kill him!

1564
02:31:46,514 --> 02:31:50,382
You are the luckiest, the canniest...

1565
02:31:50,476 --> 02:31:54,515
...and the most reckless man
I ever knew.

1566
02:31:55,189 --> 02:31:56,679
Bless you, laddie.

1567
02:31:57,275 --> 02:31:59,015
Gimli, where is the king?

1568
02:32:08,036 --> 02:32:09,025
[IN ELVISH]

1569
02:32:12,790 --> 02:32:14,121
[IN ENGLISH]
You look terrible.

1570
02:32:41,194 --> 02:32:44,027
[SPEAKS IN ELVISH]

1571
02:32:49,494 --> 02:32:50,529
[DOORS OPENING]

1572
02:32:55,875 --> 02:32:57,957
A great host, you say?

1573
02:32:58,044 --> 02:32:59,580
[IN ENGLISH]
All Isengard is emptied.

1574
02:32:59,671 --> 02:33:00,751
How many?

1575
02:33:01,422 --> 02:33:04,414
ARAGORN:
Ten thousand strong at least.

1576
02:33:05,968 --> 02:33:07,424
Ten thousand?

1577
02:33:07,845 --> 02:33:10,336
It is an army bred for a single purpose:

1578
02:33:13,017 --> 02:33:15,133
To destroy the world of Men.

1579
02:33:17,647 --> 02:33:19,638
They will be here by nightfall.

1580
02:33:25,488 --> 02:33:26,773
Let them come!

1581
02:33:28,282 --> 02:33:31,115
I want every man and strong lad
able to bear arms...

1582
02:33:31,202 --> 02:33:34,365
...to be ready for battle by nightfall.

1583
02:33:42,630 --> 02:33:45,588
We will cover the causeway
and the gate from above.

1584
02:33:45,675 --> 02:33:48,166
No army has ever breached
the Deeping Wall...

1585
02:33:48,261 --> 02:33:51,094
...or set foot inside the Hornburg!

1586
02:33:51,180 --> 02:33:53,637
This is no rabble of mindless Orcs.

1587
02:33:54,225 --> 02:33:56,466
These are Uruk-hai.

1588
02:33:56,561 --> 02:34:00,019
Their armour is thick
and their shields broad.

1589
02:34:01,649 --> 02:34:05,358
I have fought many wars,
Master Dwarf.

1590
02:34:05,445 --> 02:34:09,108
I know how to defend my own keep.

1591
02:34:15,705 --> 02:34:19,163
They will break upon this fortress
like water on rock.

1592
02:34:19,250 --> 02:34:24,586
Saruman's hordes will pillage and burn.
We've seen it before.

1593
02:34:24,672 --> 02:34:27,414
Crops can be resown...

1594
02:34:27,508 --> 02:34:30,545
...homes rebuilt.

1595
02:34:31,179 --> 02:34:33,716
Within these walls...

1596
02:34:34,098 --> 02:34:35,634
...we will outlast them.

1597
02:34:35,725 --> 02:34:38,216
They do not come to destroy Rohan's
crops or villages.

1598
02:34:38,311 --> 02:34:39,926
They come to destroy its people...

1599
02:34:40,021 --> 02:34:42,558
...down to the last child.

1600
02:34:43,441 --> 02:34:45,727
What would you have me do?

1601
02:34:45,818 --> 02:34:47,649
Look at my men.

1602
02:34:47,737 --> 02:34:49,523
Their courage hangs by a thread.

1603
02:34:51,699 --> 02:34:56,159
If this is to be our end, then I would
have them make such an end...

1604
02:34:56,245 --> 02:34:59,328
...as to be worthy of remembrance.

1605
02:35:02,960 --> 02:35:04,871
ARAGORN:
Send out riders, my lord.

1606
02:35:05,171 --> 02:35:08,038
You must call for aid.

1607
02:35:11,302 --> 02:35:13,543
And who will come?

1608
02:35:13,971 --> 02:35:15,586
Elves?

1609
02:35:15,681 --> 02:35:17,797
Dwarves?

1610
02:35:18,559 --> 02:35:21,426
We are not so lucky in our friends
as you.

1611
02:35:22,271 --> 02:35:24,557
The old alliances are dead.

1612
02:35:24,982 --> 02:35:27,815
-Gondor will answer.
-Gondor?!

1613
02:35:27,902 --> 02:35:30,143
Where was Gondor
when the Westfold fell?!

1614
02:35:31,113 --> 02:35:34,401
Where was Gondor when
our enemies closed in around us?!

1615
02:35:34,492 --> 02:35:36,448
Where was Gon--?

1616
02:35:39,121 --> 02:35:41,077
No, my Lord Aragorn...

1617
02:35:42,667 --> 02:35:45,124
...we are alone.

1618
02:35:52,009 --> 02:35:53,795
Get the women and children
into the caves.

1619
02:35:53,886 --> 02:35:55,217
MAN 1: We need more time
to lay provisions--

1620
02:35:55,304 --> 02:35:58,842
THÉODEN:
There is no time. War is upon us.

1621
02:35:59,100 --> 02:36:00,806
MAN 2:
Secure the gate.

1622
02:36:01,477 --> 02:36:04,389
[CAWING]

1623
02:36:06,023 --> 02:36:08,184
We Ents have not troubled...

1624
02:36:08,276 --> 02:36:11,689
...about the wars of Men and wizards...

1625
02:36:12,446 --> 02:36:15,438
...for a very long time.

1626
02:36:16,701 --> 02:36:21,491
But now, something
is about to happen...

1627
02:36:21,581 --> 02:36:24,038
...that has not happened...

1628
02:36:24,125 --> 02:36:26,616
...for an age.

1629
02:36:27,837 --> 02:36:30,123
Entmoot.

1630
02:36:30,506 --> 02:36:31,541
What's that?

1631
02:36:31,966 --> 02:36:34,799
'Tis a gathering.

1632
02:36:35,970 --> 02:36:38,552
A gathering of what?

1633
02:36:38,848 --> 02:36:41,885
[RUMBLING]

1634
02:36:56,490 --> 02:36:58,856
TREEBEARD:
Beech. Oak.

1635
02:36:58,951 --> 02:37:00,907
Chestnut. Ash.

1636
02:37:01,162 --> 02:37:03,198
Good. Good. Good.

1637
02:37:03,289 --> 02:37:05,655
Many have come.

1638
02:37:13,215 --> 02:37:16,048
Now we must decide
if the Ents...

1639
02:37:16,135 --> 02:37:18,717
...will go to war.

1640
02:37:27,688 --> 02:37:30,725
GUARD 1:
Move back! Move to the caves!

1641
02:37:33,194 --> 02:37:35,276
GUARD 2:
Come on, people! Quickly, now!

1642
02:37:35,696 --> 02:37:38,028
We'll place the reserves along the wall.

1643
02:37:38,115 --> 02:37:40,481
They can support the archers
from above the gate.

1644
02:37:40,576 --> 02:37:43,784
Aragorn, you must rest.

1645
02:37:43,871 --> 02:37:45,452
You're no use to us half alive.

1646
02:37:45,539 --> 02:37:46,654
[BABY CRYING]

1647
02:37:46,749 --> 02:37:47,989
ÉOWYN:
Aragorn!

1648
02:37:51,379 --> 02:37:54,462
I'm to be sent with the women
into the caves.

1649
02:37:54,548 --> 02:37:56,288
That is an honorable charge.

1650
02:37:56,384 --> 02:37:59,342
To mind the children, to find food
and bedding when the men return.

1651
02:37:59,428 --> 02:38:01,214
What renown is there in that?

1652
02:38:01,305 --> 02:38:05,048
My lady, a time may come for valor
without renown.

1653
02:38:05,309 --> 02:38:08,142
Who then will your people look to
in the last defense?

1654
02:38:08,229 --> 02:38:13,269
-Let me stand at your side.
-It is not in my power to command it.

1655
02:38:13,567 --> 02:38:16,434
You do not command
the others to stay!

1656
02:38:16,529 --> 02:38:20,317
They fight beside you because they
would not be parted from you.

1657
02:38:21,492 --> 02:38:23,699
Because they love you.

1658
02:38:30,793 --> 02:38:32,329
I'm sorry.

1659
02:38:43,806 --> 02:38:45,671
[BABY CRYING]

1660
02:39:09,248 --> 02:39:12,206
[MUTED SPEECH]

1661
02:39:27,767 --> 02:39:31,100
[CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY]

1662
02:39:38,235 --> 02:39:41,523
Farmers, farriers, stable boys.

1663
02:39:42,615 --> 02:39:44,401
These are no soldiers.

1664
02:39:46,660 --> 02:39:50,152
-Most have seen too many winters.
-Or too few.

1665
02:39:54,085 --> 02:39:57,043
Look at them. They're frightened.

1666
02:39:57,129 --> 02:39:58,619
I can see it in their eyes.

1667
02:40:03,844 --> 02:40:05,835
[IN ELVISH]

1668
02:40:10,851 --> 02:40:12,967
[IN ELVISH]

1669
02:40:13,062 --> 02:40:14,347
Aragorn.

1670
02:40:19,568 --> 02:40:21,775
[IN ENGLISH]
Then I shall die as one of them!

1671
02:40:28,202 --> 02:40:30,033
GIMLI:
Let him go, lad.

1672
02:40:30,621 --> 02:40:32,532
Let him be.

1673
02:40:34,041 --> 02:40:39,536
Every villager able to wield a sword
has been sent to the armoury.

1674
02:40:43,801 --> 02:40:45,712
My lord?

1675
02:40:47,763 --> 02:40:50,345
Who am I, Gamling?

1676
02:40:53,727 --> 02:40:57,595
You are our king, sire.

1677
02:41:00,609 --> 02:41:03,851
And do you trust your king?

1678
02:41:05,406 --> 02:41:08,614
Your men, my lord...

1679
02:41:08,701 --> 02:41:11,534
...will follow you to whatever end.

1680
02:41:18,419 --> 02:41:20,330
To whatever end.

1681
02:41:30,181 --> 02:41:33,799
Where is the horse and the rider?

1682
02:41:33,893 --> 02:41:36,976
Where is the horn that was blowing?

1683
02:41:38,480 --> 02:41:42,940
<i>They have passed like rain</i>
<i>on the mountains.</i>

1684
02:41:43,944 --> 02:41:47,152
<i>Like wind in the meadow.</i>

1685
02:41:50,826 --> 02:41:54,569
The days have gone down in the West...

1686
02:41:55,289 --> 02:41:57,905
<i>...behind the hills...</i>

1687
02:41:59,835 --> 02:42:01,450
<i>...into Shadow.</i>

1688
02:42:09,929 --> 02:42:13,342
How did it come to this?

1689
02:42:22,942 --> 02:42:25,775
[ENTS GROANING]

1690
02:42:29,657 --> 02:42:31,272
Huh?

1691
02:42:34,662 --> 02:42:36,493
It's been going for hours.

1692
02:42:37,665 --> 02:42:40,122
They must have decided something
by now.

1693
02:42:40,209 --> 02:42:44,373
TREEBEARD:
Decided? No.

1694
02:42:44,463 --> 02:42:49,674
We only just finished saying...

1695
02:42:50,844 --> 02:42:52,709
...good morning.

1696
02:42:54,056 --> 02:42:57,298
But it's nighttime already.

1697
02:42:57,393 --> 02:42:59,224
You can't take forever.

1698
02:43:00,229 --> 02:43:02,311
Don't be hasty.

1699
02:43:02,731 --> 02:43:05,143
We're running out of time!

1700
02:43:08,279 --> 02:43:11,112
GUARD:
Move! Move to the outer wall.

1701
02:43:28,674 --> 02:43:29,959
Give me your sword.

1702
02:43:39,476 --> 02:43:40,636
What is your name?

1703
02:43:41,228 --> 02:43:43,560
Haleth, son of Háma, my lord.

1704
02:43:45,733 --> 02:43:48,315
The men are saying that
we will not live out the night.

1705
02:43:50,321 --> 02:43:52,277
They say that it is hopeless.

1706
02:44:10,090 --> 02:44:11,705
This is a good sword.

1707
02:44:13,761 --> 02:44:16,093
Haleth, son of Háma...

1708
02:44:20,434 --> 02:44:22,595
...there is always hope.

1709
02:44:45,584 --> 02:44:48,997
We have trusted you this far.
You have not led us astray.

1710
02:44:49,088 --> 02:44:50,703
Forgive me.

1711
02:44:50,798 --> 02:44:52,254
I was wrong to despair.

1712
02:44:55,469 --> 02:44:57,960
[IN ELVISH]

1713
02:45:01,141 --> 02:45:04,258
We had time, I'd get this adjusted.

1714
02:45:07,731 --> 02:45:09,767
It's a little tight across the chest.

1715
02:45:12,444 --> 02:45:14,685
[HORN BLOWING]

1716
02:45:15,989 --> 02:45:17,900
That is no Orc horn.

1717
02:45:23,622 --> 02:45:25,487
Send for the king.

1718
02:45:25,582 --> 02:45:29,200
-Open the gate!
GUARD: Open up the gate!

1719
02:46:00,868 --> 02:46:02,529
How is this possible?

1720
02:46:03,537 --> 02:46:07,246
I bring word from Elrond of Rivendell.

1721
02:46:07,332 --> 02:46:10,574
An alliance once existed
between Elves and Men.

1722
02:46:11,295 --> 02:46:15,504
Long ago we fought and died together.

1723
02:46:17,801 --> 02:46:20,668
We come to honor that allegiance.

1724
02:46:21,138 --> 02:46:23,379
[SPEAKING IN ELVISH]

1725
02:46:29,188 --> 02:46:31,099
[IN ENGLISH]
You are most welcome.

1726
02:46:36,487 --> 02:46:40,275
We are proud to fight
alongside Men once more.

1727
02:47:02,554 --> 02:47:06,422
[MARCHING FOOTSTEPS
APPROACHING]

1728
02:47:06,767 --> 02:47:10,100
[INDISTINCT GRUNTING
AND GROWLING]

1729
02:47:14,066 --> 02:47:17,308
GIMLI:
You could have picked a better spot.

1730
02:47:22,157 --> 02:47:26,366
Well, lad, whatever luck you live by,
let's hope it lasts the night.

1731
02:47:27,579 --> 02:47:29,535
[THUNDER ROLLS]

1732
02:47:32,501 --> 02:47:34,287
Your friends are with you, Aragorn.

1733
02:47:34,920 --> 02:47:37,411
Let's hope they last the night.

1734
02:47:40,384 --> 02:47:43,251
[THUNDER RUMBLING]

1735
02:48:12,374 --> 02:48:15,411
[MARCHING FOOTSTEPS
APPROACHING]

1736
02:48:19,965 --> 02:48:21,626
[BABY CRYING]

1737
02:48:37,399 --> 02:48:40,061
[IN ELVISH]

1738
02:48:48,660 --> 02:48:50,946
[ROARS]

1739
02:49:18,857 --> 02:49:21,690
-What's happening out there?
-Shall I describe it to you?

1740
02:49:22,944 --> 02:49:24,730
Or would you like me to find you a box?

1741
02:49:27,783 --> 02:49:32,197
[URUK-HAI BATTLE CRIES]

1742
02:50:07,489 --> 02:50:09,480
[GROANS]

1743
02:50:27,926 --> 02:50:29,757
So it begins.

1744
02:50:45,819 --> 02:50:48,026
[IN ELVISH]

1745
02:50:56,621 --> 02:50:57,952
Did they hit anything?

1746
02:50:58,623 --> 02:51:00,659
Give them a volley.

1747
02:51:00,751 --> 02:51:02,912
-Fire!
-Fire!

1748
02:51:08,300 --> 02:51:11,758
[SPEAKS IN ELVISH]

1749
02:51:18,643 --> 02:51:20,304
Send them to me! Come on!

1750
02:51:41,124 --> 02:51:42,159
Good!

1751
02:51:48,965 --> 02:51:51,957
[IN ENGLISH]
Swords! Swords!

1752
02:52:30,048 --> 02:52:32,209
Legolas! Two already!

1753
02:52:32,300 --> 02:52:34,507
[IN ENGLISH]
I'm on 17!

1754
02:52:34,594 --> 02:52:37,210
I'll have no pointy-ear outscoring me!

1755
02:52:44,020 --> 02:52:45,726
Nineteen!

1756
02:53:07,294 --> 02:53:10,331
[ENTS GROANING]

1757
02:53:11,715 --> 02:53:13,125
Merry.

1758
02:53:17,554 --> 02:53:21,342
We have just agreed.

1759
02:53:31,359 --> 02:53:32,815
Yes?

1760
02:53:34,321 --> 02:53:38,485
I have told your names to the Entmoot...

1761
02:53:39,618 --> 02:53:42,860
...and we have agreed...

1762
02:53:43,330 --> 02:53:47,369
...you are not Orcs.

1763
02:53:49,127 --> 02:53:51,288
Well, that's good news.

1764
02:53:51,379 --> 02:53:55,543
And what about Saruman?
Have you come to a decision about him?

1765
02:53:56,176 --> 02:54:00,010
Now, don't be hasty, Master Meriadoc.

1766
02:54:00,096 --> 02:54:01,677
Hasty?

1767
02:54:02,474 --> 02:54:04,385
Our friends are out there.

1768
02:54:04,476 --> 02:54:08,685
They need our help. They cannot
fight this war on their own.

1769
02:54:09,022 --> 02:54:11,354
War? Yes.

1770
02:54:11,441 --> 02:54:13,397
It affects us all.

1771
02:54:13,485 --> 02:54:16,522
Tree, root and twig.

1772
02:54:17,405 --> 02:54:21,523
But you must understand, young Hobbit...

1773
02:54:21,618 --> 02:54:23,609
...it takes a long time...

1774
02:54:23,703 --> 02:54:28,697
...to say anything in Old Entish...

1775
02:54:28,792 --> 02:54:33,081
...and we never say anything...

1776
02:54:33,171 --> 02:54:37,164
...unless it is worth taking...

1777
02:54:37,258 --> 02:54:41,342
...a long time to say.

1778
02:54:42,138 --> 02:54:45,471
Seventeen! Eighteen!

1779
02:54:45,558 --> 02:54:46,673
Nineteen!

1780
02:54:47,227 --> 02:54:49,138
Twenty!

1781
02:54:49,229 --> 02:54:50,935
Twenty-one!

1782
02:55:01,032 --> 02:55:02,112
Causeway!

1783
02:55:02,200 --> 02:55:04,236
[ARAGORN SHOUTS IN ELVISH]

1784
02:55:10,792 --> 02:55:13,204
Is this it?

1785
02:55:13,294 --> 02:55:16,252
Is this all you can conjure, Saruman?

1786
02:55:42,657 --> 02:55:43,988
[IN ELVISH]

1787
02:56:42,258 --> 02:56:43,623
Brace the gate!

1788
02:57:01,945 --> 02:57:04,186
Hold them! Stand firm!

1789
02:57:12,080 --> 02:57:13,411
Aragorn!

1790
02:57:18,044 --> 02:57:19,250
Gimli!

1791
02:57:25,510 --> 02:57:26,966
[SPEAKS IN ELVISH]

1792
02:57:29,889 --> 02:57:30,878
[IN ELVISH]

1793
02:58:08,011 --> 02:58:11,924
The Ents cannot hold back this storm.

1794
02:58:12,724 --> 02:58:16,717
We must weather such things
as we have always done.

1795
02:58:17,562 --> 02:58:19,644
How can that be your decision?!

1796
02:58:20,315 --> 02:58:23,933
This is not our war.

1797
02:58:24,235 --> 02:58:26,442
But you're part of this world!

1798
02:58:30,575 --> 02:58:32,406
Aren't you?!

1799
02:58:33,369 --> 02:58:36,076
[ENTS GRUMBLING]

1800
02:58:36,497 --> 02:58:38,863
You must help. Please.

1801
02:58:40,168 --> 02:58:42,910
You must do something.

1802
02:58:43,213 --> 02:58:47,502
You are young and brave, Master Merry.

1803
02:58:48,718 --> 02:58:52,461
But your part in this tale is over.

1804
02:58:52,555 --> 02:58:54,841
Go back to your home.

1805
02:59:04,859 --> 02:59:07,145
Maybe Treebeard's right.

1806
02:59:07,237 --> 02:59:09,193
We don't belong here, Merry.

1807
02:59:09,280 --> 02:59:11,646
It's too big for us.

1808
02:59:11,741 --> 02:59:14,448
What can we do in the end?

1809
02:59:16,746 --> 02:59:19,362
We've got the Shire.

1810
02:59:19,916 --> 02:59:22,453
Maybe we should go home.

1811
02:59:24,295 --> 02:59:27,537
The fires of Isengard will spread...

1812
02:59:27,632 --> 02:59:32,626
...and the woods of Tuckborough
and Buckland will burn.

1813
02:59:32,720 --> 02:59:34,335
And....

1814
02:59:36,140 --> 02:59:39,223
And all that was once green and good
in this world will be gone.

1815
02:59:42,772 --> 02:59:45,684
There won't be a Shire, Pippin.

1816
03:00:05,211 --> 03:00:06,496
GAMLING:
Aragorn!

1817
03:00:06,587 --> 03:00:09,044
Fall back to the Keep!

1818
03:00:09,132 --> 03:00:12,249
Get your men out of there!

1819
03:00:13,386 --> 03:00:14,876
[IN ELVISH]

1820
03:00:21,894 --> 03:00:23,555
Haldir!

1821
03:00:27,692 --> 03:00:30,934
GIMLI: What are you doing?
What are you stopping for?

1822
03:00:31,195 --> 03:00:33,356
[SHOUTING IN ELVISH]

1823
03:00:50,173 --> 03:00:51,379
Haldir!

1824
03:01:34,092 --> 03:01:35,582
MAN:
Brace the gate!

1825
03:01:37,804 --> 03:01:39,089
Hold them!

1826
03:01:40,932 --> 03:01:44,299
To the gate. Draw your swords!

1827
03:02:12,463 --> 03:02:14,374
Make way!

1828
03:02:17,301 --> 03:02:19,007
We cannot hold much longer!

1829
03:02:24,976 --> 03:02:28,594
THÉODEN: Hold them!
-How long do you need?

1830
03:02:28,688 --> 03:02:31,350
As long as you can give me.

1831
03:02:31,441 --> 03:02:33,147
Gimli!

1832
03:02:34,610 --> 03:02:36,020
Timbers!

1833
03:02:36,112 --> 03:02:38,103
MAN:
Brace the gate!

1834
03:02:52,879 --> 03:02:54,585
Come on. We can take them.

1835
03:02:55,423 --> 03:02:57,038
It's a long way.

1836
03:03:02,305 --> 03:03:04,045
Toss me.

1837
03:03:05,224 --> 03:03:07,089
-What?
-I cannot jump the distance!

1838
03:03:07,185 --> 03:03:08,800
You'll have to toss me!

1839
03:03:14,400 --> 03:03:15,685
Don't tell the Elf.

1840
03:03:16,194 --> 03:03:17,980
Not a word.

1841
03:03:33,211 --> 03:03:34,701
Shore up the door!

1842
03:03:34,795 --> 03:03:36,956
MAN 1: Make way!
MAN 2: Follow me to the barricade.

1843
03:03:37,048 --> 03:03:38,163
MAN 1:
Watch our backs!

1844
03:03:42,303 --> 03:03:44,544
MAN 3: Throw another one over here!
-Higher!

1845
03:04:34,480 --> 03:04:35,890
MAN 4:
Hold fast the gate!

1846
03:04:40,111 --> 03:04:43,069
Gimli! Aragorn!
Get out of there!

1847
03:04:47,785 --> 03:04:49,400
Aragorn!

1848
03:05:22,820 --> 03:05:25,277
Pull everybody back.

1849
03:05:25,656 --> 03:05:27,442
Pull them back.

1850
03:05:27,992 --> 03:05:29,482
Fall back!

1851
03:05:29,577 --> 03:05:32,114
Fall back!

1852
03:05:33,289 --> 03:05:34,904
THÉODEN:
They have broken through!

1853
03:05:34,999 --> 03:05:37,456
The castle is breached. Retreat!

1854
03:05:37,543 --> 03:05:39,875
GAMLING: Fall back!
THÉODEN: Retreat!

1855
03:05:39,962 --> 03:05:42,624
ARAGORN:
Hurry! Inside. Get them inside!

1856
03:05:42,715 --> 03:05:45,001
THÉODEN:
Into the Keep!

1857
03:05:56,479 --> 03:06:01,473
I will leave you at the western borders
of the forest.

1858
03:06:01,567 --> 03:06:06,311
You can make your way north
to your homeland from there.

1859
03:06:12,036 --> 03:06:13,321
Wait! Stop!

1860
03:06:14,205 --> 03:06:15,695
Stop!

1861
03:06:18,834 --> 03:06:20,540
Turn around.

1862
03:06:21,462 --> 03:06:24,204
-Turn around. Take us south.
-South?

1863
03:06:24,298 --> 03:06:29,338
But that will lead you past Isengard.

1864
03:06:29,679 --> 03:06:32,421
Yes. Exactly.

1865
03:06:32,515 --> 03:06:35,803
If we go south, we can slip
past Saruman unnoticed.

1866
03:06:35,893 --> 03:06:38,635
The closer we are to danger,
the farther we are from harm.

1867
03:06:38,729 --> 03:06:40,765
It's the last thing he'll expect.

1868
03:06:43,401 --> 03:06:46,438
That doesn't make sense to me.

1869
03:06:46,529 --> 03:06:47,769
But then...

1870
03:06:47,863 --> 03:06:50,605
...you are very small.

1871
03:06:51,075 --> 03:06:52,861
Perhaps you're right.

1872
03:06:55,496 --> 03:06:57,032
South it is, then.

1873
03:06:58,541 --> 03:07:01,874
Hold on, little Shirelings.

1874
03:07:03,921 --> 03:07:06,708
I always like going south.

1875
03:07:06,799 --> 03:07:11,133
Somehow it feels like going downhill.

1876
03:07:11,762 --> 03:07:14,253
Are you mad? We'll be caught.

1877
03:07:14,348 --> 03:07:16,304
No, we won't.

1878
03:07:17,059 --> 03:07:19,300
Not this time.

1879
03:07:25,943 --> 03:07:26,978
MAN:
Look!

1880
03:07:28,612 --> 03:07:31,103
Osgiliath burns!

1881
03:07:31,198 --> 03:07:32,654
Mordor has come.

1882
03:07:33,784 --> 03:07:36,196
The Ring will not save Gondor.

1883
03:07:37,538 --> 03:07:39,745
It has only the power to destroy.

1884
03:07:40,624 --> 03:07:42,114
Please...

1885
03:07:42,209 --> 03:07:43,870
...let me go.

1886
03:07:44,920 --> 03:07:46,501
Hurry.

1887
03:07:49,967 --> 03:07:51,423
FRODO:
Faramir!

1888
03:07:51,510 --> 03:07:53,876
You must let me go!

1889
03:07:54,472 --> 03:07:57,964
TREEBEARD:
And those little family of field mice...

1890
03:07:58,058 --> 03:08:00,925
...that climb up sometimes,
and they tickle me awfully.

1891
03:08:01,645 --> 03:08:04,978
They're always trying to get somewhere
where they....

1892
03:08:05,399 --> 03:08:07,731
[GASPS]

1893
03:08:16,160 --> 03:08:19,072
Many of these trees were my friends.

1894
03:08:19,789 --> 03:08:24,408
Creatures I had known
from nut and acorn.

1895
03:08:25,586 --> 03:08:26,826
I'm sorry, Treebeard.

1896
03:08:26,921 --> 03:08:29,708
They had voices of their own.

1897
03:08:31,967 --> 03:08:34,504
Saruman.

1898
03:08:34,845 --> 03:08:37,928
A wizard should know better!

1899
03:08:40,351 --> 03:08:43,263
[ROARING]

1900
03:08:52,196 --> 03:08:55,905
There is no curse in Elvish...

1901
03:08:55,991 --> 03:08:58,733
...Entish or the tongues of Men...

1902
03:08:58,828 --> 03:09:01,194
...for this treachery.

1903
03:09:02,623 --> 03:09:05,456
Look! The trees! They're moving!

1904
03:09:10,172 --> 03:09:11,378
Where are they going?

1905
03:09:11,882 --> 03:09:15,124
They have business with the Orcs.

1906
03:09:15,594 --> 03:09:19,928
My business is with Isengard tonight...

1907
03:09:20,015 --> 03:09:22,677
...with rock and stone.

1908
03:09:23,060 --> 03:09:26,973
[GROANING AND FOOTSTEPS
APPROACHING]

1909
03:09:46,584 --> 03:09:47,744
Yes.

1910
03:09:48,836 --> 03:09:50,246
TREEBEARD:
Come, my friends.

1911
03:09:51,589 --> 03:09:55,832
The Ents are going to war.

1912
03:09:55,926 --> 03:09:57,791
It is likely...

1913
03:09:57,887 --> 03:10:01,425
...that we go to our doom.

1914
03:10:02,850 --> 03:10:05,307
Last march...

1915
03:10:05,853 --> 03:10:07,889
...of the Ents.

1916
03:10:55,986 --> 03:10:59,774
Faramir! Orcs have taken the eastern
shore. Their numbers are too great.

1917
03:10:59,865 --> 03:11:01,981
By nightfall we will be overrun.

1918
03:11:04,745 --> 03:11:06,201
Mr. Frodo?

1919
03:11:06,497 --> 03:11:10,661
It's calling to him, Sam.
His Eye is almost on me.

1920
03:11:10,751 --> 03:11:13,288
Hold on, Mr. Frodo.
You'll be all right.

1921
03:11:15,798 --> 03:11:18,665
[MUTED SPEECH]

1922
03:11:27,601 --> 03:11:29,011
Take them to my father.

1923
03:11:30,562 --> 03:11:33,554
Tell him Faramir sends a mighty gift.

1924
03:11:35,985 --> 03:11:39,022
A weapon that will change our fortunes
in this war.

1925
03:11:40,197 --> 03:11:42,859
Do you want to know
what happened to Boromir?

1926
03:11:43,534 --> 03:11:46,276
You want to know
why your brother died?

1927
03:11:46,787 --> 03:11:50,575
He tried to take the Ring from Frodo
after swearing an oath to protect him!

1928
03:11:50,666 --> 03:11:52,622
He tried to kill him!

1929
03:11:52,710 --> 03:11:55,076
The Ring drove your brother mad!

1930
03:11:55,879 --> 03:11:57,710
ITHILIEN RANGER:
Watch out!

1931
03:12:05,389 --> 03:12:08,347
[RUMBLING]

1932
03:12:08,642 --> 03:12:09,757
Mr. Frodo?

1933
03:12:12,396 --> 03:12:14,227
They're here.

1934
03:12:17,359 --> 03:12:19,816
They've come.

1935
03:12:20,446 --> 03:12:22,061
[RINGWRAITH SCREECHING]

1936
03:12:22,406 --> 03:12:24,362
Nazgûl!

1937
03:12:24,450 --> 03:12:26,782
[ROARING]

1938
03:12:46,430 --> 03:12:48,591
Stay here. Keep out of sight.

1939
03:12:50,392 --> 03:12:52,599
Take cover!

1940
03:13:09,953 --> 03:13:11,489
THÉODEN:
The fortress is taken.

1941
03:13:12,289 --> 03:13:13,495
It is over.

1942
03:13:13,582 --> 03:13:17,621
You said this fortress would never fall
while your men defend it.

1943
03:13:17,711 --> 03:13:20,669
They still defend it.
They have died defending it.

1944
03:13:23,425 --> 03:13:24,790
WOMAN 1:
They're breaking in!

1945
03:13:27,471 --> 03:13:29,962
WOMAN 2:
They're past the door!

1946
03:13:33,310 --> 03:13:37,394
Is there no other way for the women
and children to get out of the caves?

1947
03:13:40,109 --> 03:13:42,020
Is there no other way?

1948
03:13:43,612 --> 03:13:46,649
There is one passage.
It leads into the mountains.

1949
03:13:47,324 --> 03:13:49,531
But they will not get far.
The Uruk-hai are too many.

1950
03:13:54,414 --> 03:13:56,871
Tell the women and children
to make for the mountain pass.

1951
03:13:56,959 --> 03:13:59,826
-And barricade the entrance!
-So much death.

1952
03:14:02,005 --> 03:14:05,418
What can Men do
against such reckless hate?

1953
03:14:10,097 --> 03:14:11,507
Ride out with me.

1954
03:14:15,644 --> 03:14:17,259
Ride out and meet them.

1955
03:14:18,021 --> 03:14:20,228
For death and glory.

1956
03:14:20,315 --> 03:14:21,771
For Rohan.

1957
03:14:23,277 --> 03:14:24,733
For your people.

1958
03:14:25,487 --> 03:14:27,398
The sun is rising.

1959
03:14:31,910 --> 03:14:34,947
GANDALF: <i>Look to my coming</i>
<i>at first light on the fifth day.</i>

1960
03:14:35,038 --> 03:14:36,528
<i>At dawn...</i>

1961
03:14:36,623 --> 03:14:38,363
<i>...look to the east.</i>

1962
03:14:42,546 --> 03:14:44,207
Yes.

1963
03:14:46,675 --> 03:14:48,336
Yes.

1964
03:14:49,678 --> 03:14:52,090
The horn of Helm Hammerhand...

1965
03:14:52,181 --> 03:14:55,048
...shall sound in the Deep...

1966
03:14:55,475 --> 03:14:57,511
...one last time.

1967
03:14:57,603 --> 03:14:59,139
Yes!

1968
03:15:02,191 --> 03:15:05,979
Let this be the hour
when we draw swords together.

1969
03:15:13,744 --> 03:15:15,075
Fell deeds, awake.

1970
03:15:16,288 --> 03:15:17,448
Now for wrath...

1971
03:15:17,539 --> 03:15:20,952
...now for ruin and a red dawn.

1972
03:15:21,585 --> 03:15:24,622
[HORN BLOWS]

1973
03:15:28,008 --> 03:15:30,249
Forth Eorlingas!

1974
03:15:30,552 --> 03:15:32,918
[BATTLE CRIES]

1975
03:16:13,428 --> 03:16:15,293
[HORSE NEIGHS]

1976
03:16:18,058 --> 03:16:19,298
Gandalf.

1977
03:16:26,566 --> 03:16:30,229
Théoden King stands alone.

1978
03:16:30,821 --> 03:16:32,982
Not alone.

1979
03:16:33,407 --> 03:16:34,522
Rohirrim!

1980
03:16:40,455 --> 03:16:41,661
Éomer.

1981
03:16:41,748 --> 03:16:44,330
To the king!

1982
03:18:01,912 --> 03:18:03,698
Yes!

1983
03:18:04,247 --> 03:18:05,453
[GRUNTS]

1984
03:18:07,417 --> 03:18:09,749
[ENTS ROARING]

1985
03:18:12,839 --> 03:18:16,172
TREEBEARD:
A hit. A fine hit.

1986
03:18:16,259 --> 03:18:17,339
[TREEBEARD GRUNTS]

1987
03:18:40,826 --> 03:18:43,317
TREEBEARD:
Break the dam!

1988
03:18:43,412 --> 03:18:46,904
Release the river!

1989
03:19:14,234 --> 03:19:16,976
Pippin! Hold on!

1990
03:19:22,242 --> 03:19:25,154
Hold on, little Hobbits.

1991
03:20:06,536 --> 03:20:08,527
What are you doing?

1992
03:20:17,130 --> 03:20:18,711
Where are you going?

1993
03:20:19,883 --> 03:20:24,092
[RUMBLING]

1994
03:20:57,170 --> 03:20:59,126
[ROARING]

1995
03:21:08,223 --> 03:21:09,463
[YELLS]

1996
03:21:16,856 --> 03:21:18,187
It's me.

1997
03:21:20,694 --> 03:21:22,901
It's your Sam.

1998
03:21:27,242 --> 03:21:29,858
Don't you know your Sam?

1999
03:21:38,295 --> 03:21:39,751
[PANTING]

2000
03:21:39,838 --> 03:21:41,419
[SWORD CLANGS]

2001
03:21:47,596 --> 03:21:50,963
I can't do this, Sam.

2002
03:21:51,850 --> 03:21:53,841
I know.

2003
03:21:54,853 --> 03:21:57,219
It's all wrong.

2004
03:21:57,981 --> 03:21:59,972
By rights, we shouldn't even be here.

2005
03:22:07,407 --> 03:22:09,489
But we are.

2006
03:22:15,915 --> 03:22:18,998
It's like in the great stories, Mr. Frodo.

2007
03:22:19,085 --> 03:22:21,497
The ones that really mattered.

2008
03:22:22,547 --> 03:22:25,584
Full of darkness and danger they were.

2009
03:22:25,675 --> 03:22:28,712
And sometimes you didn't want
to know the end...

2010
03:22:28,803 --> 03:22:31,795
...because how could the end be happy?

2011
03:22:34,351 --> 03:22:36,592
<i>How could the world go back</i>
<i>to the way it was...</i>

2012
03:22:36,686 --> 03:22:40,224
<i>...when so much bad had happened?</i>

2013
03:22:41,066 --> 03:22:43,022
Victory!

2014
03:22:43,109 --> 03:22:44,724
We have victory!

2015
03:22:44,819 --> 03:22:48,858
SAM: <i>But in the end,</i>
<i>it's only a passing thing...</i>

2016
03:22:48,948 --> 03:22:50,358
<i>...this shadow.</i>

2017
03:22:50,450 --> 03:22:52,907
<i>Even darkness must pass.</i>

2018
03:22:52,994 --> 03:22:55,781
<i>A new day will come.</i>

2019
03:22:55,872 --> 03:22:59,865
<i>And when the sun shines,</i>
<i>it will shine out the clearer.</i>

2020
03:23:01,795 --> 03:23:04,207
<i>Those were the stories</i>
<i>that stayed with you...</i>

2021
03:23:04,297 --> 03:23:06,128
<i>...that meant something.</i>

2022
03:23:06,216 --> 03:23:08,832
<i>Even if you were too small</i>
<i>to understand why.</i>

2023
03:23:10,220 --> 03:23:14,088
<i>But I think, Mr. Frodo, I do understand.</i>

2024
03:23:14,182 --> 03:23:15,797
<i>I know now.</i>

2025
03:23:16,643 --> 03:23:18,884
Folk in those stories...

2026
03:23:18,978 --> 03:23:23,187
...had lots of chances of turning back,
only they didn't.

2027
03:23:23,274 --> 03:23:25,560
They kept going...

2028
03:23:26,236 --> 03:23:29,478
...because they were holding
on to something.

2029
03:23:31,074 --> 03:23:33,406
What are we holding on to, Sam?

2030
03:23:45,338 --> 03:23:49,251
That there's some good
in this world, Mr. Frodo.

2031
03:23:49,551 --> 03:23:52,167
And it's worth fighting for.

2032
03:24:19,080 --> 03:24:23,369
I think at last we understand one another,
Frodo Baggins.

2033
03:24:24,127 --> 03:24:28,120
You know the laws of our country,
the laws of your father.

2034
03:24:28,214 --> 03:24:30,455
If you let them go,
your life will be forfeit.

2035
03:24:34,804 --> 03:24:36,214
Then it is forfeit.

2036
03:24:38,975 --> 03:24:40,761
Release them.

2037
03:24:49,527 --> 03:24:52,234
[HOOVES BEATING]

2038
03:24:52,822 --> 03:24:54,904
ÉOMER:
Stay out of the forest!

2039
03:24:54,991 --> 03:24:56,822
Keep away from the trees!

2040
03:25:20,058 --> 03:25:24,142
[SCREAMING AND YELLING]

2041
03:25:47,669 --> 03:25:49,500
Final count...

2042
03:25:49,587 --> 03:25:52,579
-...42.
-Forty-two?

2043
03:25:52,674 --> 03:25:58,761
Oh, that's not bad for a pointy-eared
Elvish princeling.

2044
03:25:59,556 --> 03:26:03,219
I myself am sitting pretty on 43.

2045
03:26:07,355 --> 03:26:10,643
-Forty-three.
-He was already dead.

2046
03:26:11,401 --> 03:26:13,938
-He was twitching.
-He was twitching...

2047
03:26:14,028 --> 03:26:18,692
...because he's got my ax
embedded in his nervous system!

2048
03:26:20,994 --> 03:26:25,704
MERRY: He doesn't look happy, does he?
PIPPIN: Not too happy at all, Merry.

2049
03:26:25,957 --> 03:26:29,541
Still, I suppose the view
would be quite nice from up there.

2050
03:26:29,627 --> 03:26:32,664
Oh, yes. It's a quality establishment.

2051
03:26:32,755 --> 03:26:35,622
I hear the staff are very good.

2052
03:26:41,306 --> 03:26:43,718
-What are you doing?
-Nothing.

2053
03:26:43,808 --> 03:26:48,142
-The world's back to normal, that's all.
-No, it isn't.

2054
03:26:48,229 --> 03:26:49,560
I'm starving.

2055
03:26:49,647 --> 03:26:52,810
Good luck trying to find something
decent around here.

2056
03:26:52,901 --> 03:26:56,018
Probably dead rats and moldy bread.

2057
03:27:19,969 --> 03:27:22,381
Saruman's storeroom!

2058
03:27:24,724 --> 03:27:27,511
I don't believe it.

2059
03:27:27,602 --> 03:27:29,684
It can't be.

2060
03:27:30,313 --> 03:27:33,180
-It is!
-Longbottom Leaf.

2061
03:27:34,484 --> 03:27:36,816
The finest pipe-weed in South Farthing.

2062
03:27:37,153 --> 03:27:40,316
It's perfect. One barrel each.

2063
03:27:40,406 --> 03:27:41,566
Wait.

2064
03:27:42,325 --> 03:27:43,565
Do you think we should share it
with Treebeard?

2065
03:27:43,660 --> 03:27:45,241
Share it?

2066
03:27:47,080 --> 03:27:49,492
No. No.

2067
03:27:51,000 --> 03:27:52,331
Dead plant and all that.

2068
03:27:52,752 --> 03:27:54,913
Don't think he'd understand.

2069
03:27:56,172 --> 03:27:58,379
Could be a distant relative.

2070
03:27:59,175 --> 03:28:01,712
I get it.

2071
03:28:01,803 --> 03:28:04,670
Don't be hasty.

2072
03:28:05,765 --> 03:28:07,505
Exactly.

2073
03:28:08,601 --> 03:28:10,842
Bar-hrum.

2074
03:28:12,689 --> 03:28:14,680
[HOBBITS LAUGHING]

2075
03:28:36,504 --> 03:28:37,835
This is the old sewer.

2076
03:28:37,922 --> 03:28:41,130
Runs right under the river
through to the edge of the city.

2077
03:28:41,217 --> 03:28:43,003
You'll find cover in the woods there.

2078
03:28:44,053 --> 03:28:46,544
Captain Faramir...

2079
03:28:47,181 --> 03:28:49,012
...you have shown your quality, sir.

2080
03:28:51,519 --> 03:28:52,804
The very highest.

2081
03:28:53,312 --> 03:28:55,974
The Shire must truly be a great realm,
Master Gamgee...

2082
03:28:56,065 --> 03:28:59,057
...where gardeners are held in high honor.

2083
03:29:00,236 --> 03:29:02,227
What road will you take
once you reach the woods?

2084
03:29:02,822 --> 03:29:04,437
Gollum says there's a path...

2085
03:29:04,532 --> 03:29:08,491
...near Minas Morgul
that climbs up into the mountains.

2086
03:29:08,953 --> 03:29:10,693
Cirith Ungol?

2087
03:29:14,250 --> 03:29:16,832
-Is that its name?
-No.

2088
03:29:16,919 --> 03:29:18,625
No!

2089
03:29:19,464 --> 03:29:22,456
-Yes.
-Frodo...

2090
03:29:22,842 --> 03:29:26,380
...they say a dark terror dwells
in the passes above Minas Morgul.

2091
03:29:27,263 --> 03:29:29,800
-You cannot go that way.
SMÉAGOL: It is the only way.

2092
03:29:30,141 --> 03:29:36,432
Master says we must go to Mordor,
so we must try.

2093
03:29:37,940 --> 03:29:39,726
I must.

2094
03:29:43,279 --> 03:29:46,897
Go, Frodo.
Go with the goodwill of all Men.

2095
03:29:46,991 --> 03:29:49,073
Thank you.

2096
03:30:00,880 --> 03:30:04,998
May death find you quickly
if you bring them to harm.

2097
03:30:17,480 --> 03:30:19,016
SAM:
Come on, keep up.

2098
03:30:22,485 --> 03:30:25,272
Mr. Frodo didn't mean for them Rangers
to hurt you.

2099
03:30:25,905 --> 03:30:27,736
You know that, don't you?

2100
03:30:28,533 --> 03:30:30,114
He was trying to save you, see?

2101
03:30:30,618 --> 03:30:32,154
Save me?

2102
03:30:32,495 --> 03:30:34,702
So there's no hard feelings.

2103
03:30:34,789 --> 03:30:40,000
-Forgive and forget.
-No, no, no hard feelings.

2104
03:30:40,086 --> 03:30:42,748
Gollum, Gollum.

2105
03:30:43,798 --> 03:30:45,538
Nice master.

2106
03:30:46,634 --> 03:30:49,501
-Nice Hobbits.
SAM: Very decent of you.

2107
03:30:49,595 --> 03:30:51,927
Very decent, indeed, Gollum.

2108
03:30:57,436 --> 03:31:02,647
Sauron's wrath will be terrible,
his retribution swift.

2109
03:31:04,443 --> 03:31:07,776
[RUMBLING]

2110
03:31:09,782 --> 03:31:12,774
GANDALF:
The battle for Helm's Deep is over.

2111
03:31:13,452 --> 03:31:16,990
The battle for Middle-earth
is about to begin.

2112
03:31:22,128 --> 03:31:25,541
All our hopes now lie
with two little Hobbits...

2113
03:31:26,549 --> 03:31:29,757
<i>...somewhere in the wilderness.</i>

2114
03:31:33,055 --> 03:31:36,513
I wonder if we'll ever be
put into songs or tales.

2115
03:31:36,601 --> 03:31:38,057
What?

2116
03:31:38,144 --> 03:31:42,183
I wonder if people will ever say,
"Let's hear about Frodo and the Ring."

2117
03:31:42,273 --> 03:31:45,606
And they'll say,
"Yes! That's one of my favorite stories."

2118
03:31:45,693 --> 03:31:48,730
"Frodo was really courageous,
wasn't he, Dad?"

2119
03:31:48,821 --> 03:31:50,561
"Yes, my boy.

2120
03:31:50,656 --> 03:31:54,524
The most famousest of Hobbits.
And that's saying a lot."

2121
03:31:54,619 --> 03:31:57,235
Well, you've left out
one of the chief characters:

2122
03:31:57,330 --> 03:31:59,286
"Samwise the Brave."

2123
03:31:59,373 --> 03:32:02,160
I want to hear more about Sam.

2124
03:32:06,464 --> 03:32:09,456
Frodo wouldn't have got far
without Sam.

2125
03:32:10,801 --> 03:32:14,840
Now, Mr. Frodo, you shouldn't make fun.
I was being serious.

2126
03:32:15,932 --> 03:32:17,297
So was I.

2127
03:32:26,192 --> 03:32:28,899
"Samwise the Brave."

2128
03:32:33,157 --> 03:32:34,522
FRODO:
Sméagol?

2129
03:32:34,617 --> 03:32:37,609
SAM: We're not going to wait for you.
Come on.

2130
03:32:37,703 --> 03:32:39,694
Master.

2131
03:32:39,789 --> 03:32:42,781
Master looks after us.

2132
03:32:43,584 --> 03:32:46,417
Master wouldn't hurt us.

2133
03:32:46,504 --> 03:32:49,041
GOLLUM:
Master broke his promise.

2134
03:32:49,131 --> 03:32:51,372
SMÉAGOL:
Don't ask Sméagol.

2135
03:32:51,467 --> 03:32:54,755
Poor, poor Sméagol.

2136
03:32:54,845 --> 03:32:57,757
Master betrayed us.

2137
03:32:57,848 --> 03:33:01,011
Wicked. Tricksy. False.

2138
03:33:01,102 --> 03:33:05,095
We ought to wring
his filthy little neck.

2139
03:33:05,189 --> 03:33:08,022
Kill him! Kill him!

2140
03:33:08,109 --> 03:33:09,690
Kill them both!

2141
03:33:09,777 --> 03:33:13,486
And then we take the precious...

2142
03:33:13,572 --> 03:33:17,156
...and we be the master!

2143
03:33:17,827 --> 03:33:20,534
But the fat Hobbit, he knows.

2144
03:33:20,621 --> 03:33:23,237
Eyes always watching.

2145
03:33:23,499 --> 03:33:27,083
Then we stabs them out.

2146
03:33:27,169 --> 03:33:31,754
Put out his eyeses
and make him crawl.

2147
03:33:31,841 --> 03:33:35,379
Yes. Yes. Yes.

2148
03:33:35,469 --> 03:33:38,256
Kill them both.

2149
03:33:38,347 --> 03:33:40,929
Yes. No! No!

2150
03:33:41,017 --> 03:33:44,760
It's too risky. It's too risky.

2151
03:33:45,479 --> 03:33:48,095
SAM:
Where is he? Where has he gone?

2152
03:33:48,190 --> 03:33:50,897
-Hey, Gollum! Where are you?
FRODO: Sméagol?

2153
03:33:50,985 --> 03:33:56,400
We could let her do it.

2154
03:33:57,366 --> 03:34:01,575
Yes. She could do it.

2155
03:34:01,662 --> 03:34:06,281
Yes, precious, she could.

2156
03:34:06,375 --> 03:34:12,462
And then we takes it
once they're dead.

2157
03:34:13,382 --> 03:34:15,168
Once they're dead.

2158
03:34:15,259 --> 03:34:17,295
Shh.

2159
03:34:20,639 --> 03:34:24,382
Come on, Hobbits. Long ways to go yet.

2160
03:34:24,477 --> 03:34:26,593
Sméagol will show you the way.

2161
03:34:26,687 --> 03:34:28,973
Follow me.

2162
03:34:47,416 --> 03:34:50,328
[THUNDER RUMBLING]
